{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests","id":848254,"title":"Beast Player's Guide: Suggestions? Requests?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-16T10:24:58-07:00","id":848254,"title":"Beast Player's Guide: Suggestions? Requests?","content":"Hey, folks. I'm working on the outline for the <b>Beast Player's Guide</b> right now (it keeps getting pushed to the back burner because of <b>Changeling 20th</b>, but it's still...cooking, I guess). Obviously I'm looking at including the things you'll expect to find; new powers, approaches to play, expanded discussions on Families and Hungers and so forth. I'm interested in what <i>you</i> folks want to see in a Player's Guide. What would be useful for playing <b>Beast</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:34:29-07:00","id":848262,"title":"","content":"A list of mythological monsters and possible Families would be nice, along with some more Legends and Lives. Some more example hunger preferences might be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:54:34-07:00","id":848279,"title":"","content":"A beast form hack.<br /> Some more Lair traits/ideas for making more - and for that matter, and expanded discussion on Lairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:58:54-07:00","id":848284,"title":"","content":"Expanded rules for Lairs, please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:04:58-07:00","id":848286,"title":"","content":"A new Beast family embodying the fear of clowns.<br /> <br /> More Kinship powers and crossover support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:13:51-07:00","id":848287,"title":"","content":"Some more Nightmares and Kinship Nightmares would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:44:35-07:00","id":848300,"title":"","content":"Discussion of Beast kinship with non-player monsters/weirder stuff would be cool. More Advanced and Epic Merits. More Lair stuff is nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:52:19-07:00","id":848304,"title":"","content":"Some official rules for dealing with ephemeral beings would be handy. Perhaps an optional rule that allows Beasts to perceive ephemeral creatures with whom they share Kinship? (if you have Kinship with a spirit, you can see spirits, if with a ghost, ghosts and so on)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:00:50-07:00","id":848312,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a thing I'm calling Dominions for now. Basically, it's an additional incentive feeding your Hunger rather than using Family Dinner, powers in relation to the things or people you enact your Hunger on. So maybe a Tyrant has the power to summon people or a Ravager can call up the history of a place he destroyed, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Alternative Birthrights are cool, as would be other tools to help bring the individual nightmare aspect around to the forefront-give people a way to emphasize Family over Hunger in a way, perhaps. Nothing specific in mind for this one<br /> <br /> Clearly a discussion section on what's going on with the Kinship powers, and expanding them ala Rites of Spring would be pretty cool-maybe small boonss that come when you slap Family Ties on someone, perhaps in relation to who they are. Same with Lair, and maybe finding a way to tie in a related Minions/Servants thing to it. Also, Cults-I am now a sucker for everyone having cults. Worship the dragon, a god is just a monster you bow to.<br /> <br /> An Incentive system for additional Beast behavior probably wouldn't be missed-I hesitate to bring up Changeling's Talecrafting, because that's not what I want, but something in that vaugeish ballpark feels like it has merit.<br /> <br /> More discussion on the Inheritances, their use in play, and the tragedy that they inherently are. Maybe one or two sideways changes(maybe 'retrograde' inheritances, where one becomes a vampire or a True Fae in the ways not yet implied by the Unfettered or the Rampant). As you might imagine, I have a soft spot for this one.<br /> <br /> COMMUNION WITH THE DARK MOTHER, oh my god, I can't believe it took me so long to think of it-but my default assumption was that the Dark Mother had no presence in the game until I read Tales of the Dark Mother, and now I want some kind of Once a Story Communion thing. Maybe tie that into the not-talecrafting idea? Whatever, more on this and the Dark Mother in game as Beasts can use it. Although, again, maybe this isn't a player's guide thing.<br /> <br /> Screwing around with Cosmology, maybe hands dripping with red style, give Beasts a sort of way to break boundaries down and create Places That Should Not Be.<br /> <br /> I want Beasts to continue to cement their place as both the great Uniter of monsters and the great Upsetter of settings. Beasts as a crossover element have a great way or breaking all the rules you know about the Chronicles of Darkness, and finding ways to do that within their own themes is one of the many great joys and challenges of this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:00:56-07:00","id":848313,"title":"","content":"A look at how Beasts tend to develop their Legends over time and balance Kinship with the demands of Hunger would be nice to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:30:53-07:00","id":848338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848300#post848300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discussion of Beast kinship with non-player monsters/weirder stuff would be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely this.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe some material needs to be devoted to Beast &quot;ecology&quot; - as in, what effect they have on their surroundings and <i>vice versa</i>. How the way they pursue their Hungers affects behavior of the local Mortals. Whether Beasts cause things to improve, deteriorate or do they provoke a torches and pitchforks reaction from Mortals. What kind of Heroes they attract, depending on their actions. How the Chambers of their Lairs resonate in the Material world. How their Kinships affect the life of their Kin, and how they in turn affect their surroundings.<br /> <br /> Since, among other things, Beast is about finding one's place in the world, it is important to know what this place is. It directly feeds into their growing Legends too. Though I admit, these things might very well be &quot;Storyteller's Guide&quot; material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848312#post848312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">COMMUNION WITH THE DARK MOTHER, oh my god, I can't believe it took me so long to think of it-but my default assumption was that the Dark Mother had no presence in the game until I read Tales of the Dark Mother, and now I want some kind of Once a Story Communion thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be excited for more material on the Dark Mother due to her actively promoting character development among her Children. As opposed to many short-lived Beasts, she seems to have attained both self-acceptance and self-awareness. Also, we don't know what other plans She may have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:30:58-07:00","id":848340,"title":"","content":"I agree with everything Arc just said. More Advanced and Epic Merits would be good, they're one of the more entertaining goodies to play around with. Additional Atavisms would be cool. It's hard to try and figure out what signature mythic monster abilities have been missed, because the core Atavisms and the Incarnate Inheritance cover <i>a lot </i>of them, but I'm sure there's still a few left.<br /> <br /> Alternate Birthrights sound very cool, as does expanding the details on inhabitants of the Primordial Dream besides Horrors. Also, new things for Heroes, because there's a lot of potential to make some really cool, unique, and bizarre antagonists there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:35:08-07:00","id":848344,"title":"","content":"It's not the right word for them, but something about lackeys and minions for Beasts. Heroes have them, but they're effectively cannon fodder. Beasts, on the other hand, lack the classic henchmen, people to do their bidding and further their Hungers--what giant doesn't have soldiers to bring Heroes before her throne? Beasts might have followers who get something out of the relationship (family and what not), as opposed to Heroic followers who are more just pawns. I'm not sure if that's a minor template or a merit, or if it's just guidelines on how Beasts access human resources, but it feels like a trope worth exploring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:37:05-07:00","id":848345,"title":"","content":"As Arc said, reasons to go for the traditional feeding rather than Family Dinner would be extremely appreciated. Be they through a new type of power, merits based around feeding yourself to gain more power, I'd be more than happy with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:57:06-07:00","id":848358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848344#post848344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the right word for them, but something about lackeys and minions for Beasts. Heroes have them, but they're effectively cannon fodder. Beasts, on the other hand, lack the classic henchmen, people to do their bidding and further their Hungers--what giant doesn't have soldiers to bring Heroes before her throne? Beasts might have followers who get something out of the relationship (family and what not), as opposed to Heroic followers who are more just pawns. I'm not sure if that's a minor template or a merit, or if it's just guidelines on how Beasts access human resources, but it feels like a trope worth exploring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I disagree with you, but it's worth mentioning that Kinship is the original facilitator of this.<br /> <br /> Still, there is a good opening for a bottom tier minion missing, and that's something the Lair can provide, I think.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Keep in mind, folks, that this is the Player's Guide, not the Storyteller's Guide. Stuff like Heroes and Astral terrors to fight belong in the latter book, not the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-16-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:02:01-07:00","id":848366,"title":"","content":"Some things I'd love:<br /> *Some more nightmares (of all sorts) and atavisms, obviously<br /> *Some sort of 'lesser' template related to Beast would be cool to have. Maybe something like how Beasts awaken Heroes but doing so in a way closer to how Beasts themselves interact with the Primordial.<br /> *A form of Beast 'magic', kinda like how sin-eaters have ceremonies. Something to give the more mystic minded Beasts a way to collect powers that don't fit neatly into the categories of Nightmares and Atavisms<br /> *Some sort of magical object creation for Beasts. Or maybe just a power that lets them more easily use the magical objects of other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:05:33-07:00","id":848370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848358#post848358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I disagree with you, but it's worth mentioning that Kinship is the original facilitator of this.<br /> <br /> Still, there is a good opening for a bottom tier minion missing, and that's something the Lair can provide, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's sort of what I was thinking too. Minions as a Lair trait. That said, it could be something more oriented to player characters too, but you're quite right that Kinship fills the function pretty well in the abstract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:05:49-07:00","id":848371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848345#post848345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Arc said, reasons to go for the traditional feeding rather than Family Dinner would be extremely appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it's worth remembering that the primary motivation that currently exists along this axis is the rising cost of upkeep over time as your Lair expands \u2014 even if you never spend Satiety on anything else, your Dinner-based options eventually boil down to spreading yourself thin on multiple drips or reducing your family to feeding conduits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:13:33-07:00","id":848376,"title":"","content":"In addition to everything Arc said and exploration of Legend and Kinship, I really want to see more on the Primordial Dream as an environment and ecosystem and specific instances of the impact it can have on the world in addition to Beasts and Heroes. A deeper look at how both deal with the Dream and the relationship of the Begotten to the rest of the Astral would be great. Also, if there's room for it, more on dreamers. What happens to a proto-Beast who <i>refuses</i> her own primordial self? How does the experience of Beasts-to-be with it differ from dormant Heroes or from Beasts who, for some odd reason or tragic twist, never come to be? Are there <i>other dreamers </i>still in these modern times where the lessons of fear are drowned by the bluster of numberless humans?<br /> <br /> I guess a lot of this sounds more like ST Guide material though. (&lt;,&lt;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-16-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:16:38-07:00","id":848380,"title":"","content":"A suicide/suicide allegory free rendition of Inheritances for those of us that are sensitive to that topic (I've some hacks for this incoming).<br /> <br /> More details on Horrors a la I'm out and about in the Primordial Dream and run across someone else's Horror. What's that even like? Would it try to snack on me?<br /> <br /> Huge +1 for Arcane Arts' alt Inheritances (with suicide free versions please).<br /> <br /> More info on the Hive, the Primordial Dream, and ephemeral things one might run into there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:21:49-07:00","id":848382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848358#post848358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I disagree with you, but it's worth mentioning that Kinship is the original facilitator of this.<br /> <br /> Still, there is a good opening for a bottom tier minion missing, and that's something the Lair can provide, I think.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Keep in mind, folks, that this is the Player's Guide, not the Storyteller's Guide. Stuff like Heroes and Astral terrors to fight belong in the latter book, not the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's also space for a merit that does this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:28:32-07:00","id":848384,"title":"","content":"I can see cults springing around Beasts for minions.<br /> <br /> Some more exploration of the story narrative of Legend and Heroes.<br /> <br /> i'll also for some kind of y Beast magic... perhaps bringing the Primordial Dream to our own world in some small ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:32:20-07:00","id":848385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848384#post848384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'll also for some kind of y Beast magic... perhaps bringing the Primordial Dream to our own world in some small ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the function of imposing Lair Traits and the reason an exceptional success on a Nightmare roll lets you make a Chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:59:00-07:00","id":848456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848380#post848380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suicide/suicide allegory free rendition of Inheritances for those of us that are sensitive to that topic (I've some hacks for this incoming).<br /> <br /> More details on Horrors a la I'm out and about in the Primordial Dream and run across someone else's Horror. What's that even like? Would it try to snack on me?<br /> <br /> Huge +1 for Arcane Arts' alt Inheritances (with suicide free versions please).<br /> <br /> More info on the Hive, the Primordial Dream, and ephemeral things one might run into there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. If anything, I would make the suicide allegory stronger and harder.<br /> <br /> Inheritances should make people cringe. Inheritances, after all, are Becoming Nightmare, it's effectively becoming a True Fae, one and all.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of words in regards to this, and I expect them to get them down this weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:11:32-07:00","id":848545,"title":"","content":"Whenever I see mention of a Player's Guide I think back to the Blood, from Vampire the Requiem, which did a great job of expanding upon the vampire experience.<br /> <br /> It was touched upon in 'The Final Nightmare' section, but really an expansion on how it <i>feels</i> to be a Beast would be useful. Vampires sense the heartbeats of everyone around them, they're still while everyone is breathing and moving and making those little tics. Werewolves see things through the lens of the predator, their senses are awash even in the real world with details of things around them. <br /> <br /> My Beast can sense sources of satiety, but what does it feel like finally being his true self? Does he feel out of place at his 9 to 5 now that the Destroyer has replaced his soul?<br /> <br /> Some expansion on the 'inherited' Horrors would be useful, too. Not the Inheritance, but when your Horror is one with 'a name and a sense of history.' Also what happens when and if the Beast and the Horror don't really mesh that well. When Angela the librarian who loves peaceful silence finds their soul inherits Aibell the Screamer, how does she deal with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:16:25-07:00","id":848550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848545#post848545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some expansion on the 'inherited' Horrors would be useful, too. Not the Inheritance, but when your Horror is one with 'a name and a sense of history.' Also what happens when and if the Beast and the Horror don't really mesh that well. When Angela the librarian who loves peaceful silence finds their soul inherits Aibell the Screamer, how does she deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. There doesn't need to mechanics tied to it, but I would like to know more about what happens when your Soul is a truly legendary beast and if these Horrors can persist through the ages. Is a Chimera Horror literally THE Chimera, one of its Offspring, or something totally unrelated. I think each of those ideas could work and coexist within the setting, but there are different implications for each one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:18:37-07:00","id":848552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848545#post848545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever I see mention of a Player's Guide I think back to the Blood, from Vampire the Requiem, which did a great job of expanding upon the vampire experience.<br /> <br /> It was touched upon in 'The Final Nightmare' section, but really an expansion on how it <i>feels</i> to be a Beast would be useful. Vampires sense the heartbeats of everyone around them, they're still while everyone is breathing and moving and making those little tics. Werewolves see things through the lens of the predator, their senses are awash even in the real world with details of things around them.<br /> <br /> My Beast can sense sources of satiety, but what does it feel like finally being his true self? Does he feel out of place at his 9 to 5 now that the Destroyer has replaced his soul?<br /> <br /> Some expansion on the 'inherited' Horrors would be useful, too. Not the Inheritance, but when your Horror is one with 'a name and a sense of history.' Also what happens when and if the Beast and the Horror don't really mesh that well. When Angela the librarian who loves peaceful silence finds their soul inherits Aibell the Screamer, how does she deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. All of this. <br /> <br /> One of my favorite books in all of the first edition of <b>Werewolf</b> was <b>Blood of the Wolf</b>, for expressly this reason.<br /> <br /> That would be pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:26:29-07:00","id":848558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848456#post848456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. If anything, I would make the suicide allegory stronger and harder.<br /> <br /> Inheritances should make people cringe. Inheritances, after all, are Becoming Nightmare, it's effectively becoming a True Fae, one and all.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of words in regards to this, and I expect them to get them down this weekend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda begs the question of why end there. If the point of the game is some nihilistic exercise why soften the Devouring, why subvert Heroes, why beat around the bush? Might as well just go for it and get your full evil on (IMO, the original draft kinda did that better).<br /> <br /> Of course it's hardly much of a subversion of anything if my end game choices are only a, b, or c.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:58:59-07:00","id":848568,"title":"","content":"Inheritance isn't an endgame, it's a way out. A Beast could reach an &quot;endgame&quot; by expanding its family and rising above the needs of Hunger. A Beast can grow in power and simply endure what life throws at it, or it can take a way out. That escape is, for all meaningful intents and purposes, false- you let the Monomyth break you and define you, either by descending into the depths of the Primordial Dream or by forcing your Horror into the world. The Unfettered and the Rampart purge their humanity and go &quot;Fine- you say I'm a monster, that I'm not a person? You're right. Let's see how you can handle it&quot;<br /> <br /> The Incarnate does something different. The world tells them they're a monster doomed to die for the benefit of the Hero, and they say &quot;Alright- I'm a monster. Let's see just how terrible a monster I can be.'<br /> <br /> Heroes are not what they seem to be either- for all but those with low Integrity, they genuinely are altruistic and benevolent, seeking out sources of fear and learning what they can from the experience. Low Integrity Heroes buy into the Legend, they can't help but think it's all about them, that the myth exists for their benefit and glory- they see the Legend as an end, and not a means to it. They refuse to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T20:01:12-07:00","id":848571,"title":"","content":"Because it's not about evil. It's about being a monster.<br /> <br /> Because, unlike Becoming Nightmare, the Inheritances are much more emotionally complex for any given Beast. To Thine Own Self Be True is challenged by the Inheritances, which ask questions about just what is the self of a Beast.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, the villain isn't the villain.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, even if the villain is the villain, it's a better choice than giving up who you are.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, your choices are inevitable, and your destiny is never certain.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, a tragedy is the sort of story you want to live, because the alternatives as emptier still.<br /> <br /> Because all the love and kindness in the world doesn't do a damn thing if a person isn't willing to move and change themselves.<br /> <br /> Because the Inheritances aren't the only endgames you have.<br /> <br /> In short, because Beast is more complicated than most people seem to get. Cough.<br /> <br /> A fuller response is coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-17-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T21:02:27-07:00","id":848594,"title":"","content":"More atavisms and nightmares. Also I think more explanation on how to use nightmares to teach lessons. Recently posted a question on denizens of the lair, I think that some method of populating the lair with things other than the Horror would be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T21:31:23-07:00","id":848600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848366#post848366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things I'd love:<br /> *A form of Beast 'magic', kinda like how sin-eaters have ceremonies. Something to give the more mystic minded Beasts a way to collect powers that don't fit neatly into the categories of Nightmares and Atavisms</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I really would like more support to play sorcerous beasts,most of really cool monsters had magical powers!<br /> morer about the Incarnate Myth. i would love to see just how strong acan get. Can an Incarnate destroy a whole city?can they use Nightmares to force no less than tens of thousands of worshippers to build an temple in his honor?i really think people would love to now more about their powers. and what Arc said about communion with the dark mother too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T22:34:59-07:00","id":848617,"title":"","content":"I want more on what it's like to <b>be</b> a beast. Like how Flowers went into the nitty gritty of the demonic condition I want to know what if feels like to have a nightmare for a soul, what it's like to explore the Primordial Dream, and what it's like to hunger for the fear and suffering of others. As someone else said further up, I'd like to know what kinship is like with something that isn't playable. What's it like being the distant cousin of a fire spirit, an azlu, or a qashmal? What's it's like having a subtle connection to the Dark Mother? A bit more about beast and demon interaction would be nice as well as we weren't able to get it in the Demon ST guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T01:53:47-07:00","id":848683,"title":"","content":"*typing this in my snazzy new Beast t-shirt*<br /> <br /> Oh boy, so much I'd like to see:<br /> - New Atavisms and Nightmares, a mix of kinship or non-kinship for the latest. New Lair Traits, Merits, etc... you name it<br /> - New powers and mechanics for Heroes. The current selection is a little bit thin.<br /> - New advice and possibly rules for exploring the astral realms outside of one's Lair. Possibly denizens of those realms as somebody suggested on these forums. In general more development on the &quot;dreamspace&quot;<br /> - Some kind of creatures/factions which are related to Beasts but neither beasts nor heroes. Something to populate the ecology, as phrased above.<br /> - Some advice on running a purely Beast campaign, contrasted with a more kinship based one. Not just one or the other, but seeing both options would be nice.<br /> - More examples, rules and context on the inheritances. <br /> - More mythology, culture, factions etc - even if historical - for Beasts.<br /> - A sub-template perhaps (what can I say I quite like these)<br /> - An in depth discussion of the five hunger groups and how they shape the psychology of Beasts. Perhaps some hunger-specific mechanics (merits, or nightmares to contrast with the Families)<br /> <br /> Aaaand that's all I can think of for now. Great to see the other answers in this thread too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T04:19:17-07:00","id":848709,"title":"","content":"I'm most interested on how the beast interact with their kin, how they interact with their societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:07:29-07:00","id":848714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848558#post848558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda begs the question of why end there. If the point of the game is some nihilistic exercise why soften the Devouring, why subvert Heroes, why beat around the bush? Might as well just go for it and get your full evil on (IMO, the original draft kinda did that better).<br /> <br /> Of course it's hardly much of a subversion of anything if my end game choices are only a, b, or c.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any other <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> game, <b>Beast</b> doesn't paint things in such easy lines as &quot;good,&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; Other games have that - first one that comes to mind is D&amp;D, obviously.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that entire discussion is a bit off-topic, and I'd suggest in general that we all get back to actually answering Matt's question posed in the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:51:24-07:00","id":848735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848600#post848600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! I really would like more support to play sorcerous beasts,most of really cool monsters had magical powers!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true and my favorite character concept was based kinda around a witch, but let's think about it: to a mortal even 'regular' Nightmares and Atavisms seem like 'magic spells', and that's not bringing in your Bestial soul and Lair imposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848312#post848312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Incentive system for additional Beast behavior probably wouldn't be missed-I hesitate to bring up Changeling's Talecrafting, because that's not what I want, but something in that vaugeish ballpark feels like it has merit....COMMUNION WITH THE DARK MOTHER</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of good ideas here from you but these two are my favorites. Something that encourages and rewards you the player indulging in the monster your character is is something I really, really want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:36:23-07:00","id":848753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848376#post848376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to see more on the Primordial Dream as an environment and ecosystem and specific instances of the impact it can have on the world in addition to Beasts and Heroes. A deeper look at how both deal with the Dream and the relationship of the Begotten to the rest of the Astral would be great. Also, if there's room for it, more on dreamers. What happens to a proto-Beast who <i>refuses</i> her own primordial self? How does the experience of Beasts-to-be with it differ from dormant Heroes or from Beasts who, for some odd reason or tragic twist, never come to be? Are there <i>other dreamers </i>still in these modern times where the lessons of fear are drowned by the bluster of numberless humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this sounds more like STGuide material than PGuide material, but I hope you (as in Matt) keep this in mind when the STGuide comes around.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see some material on building Horrors (taking a leaf from the demonic form builds perhaps - though maybe the Apocalyptic Form chapter from Demon the <i>Fallen's</i> Player's Guide would be better).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:22:18-07:00","id":848830,"title":"","content":"What everyone else has said, plus it would be awesome to get a &quot;Flowers of Hell&quot; style expanded write-up for the Families and Hungers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:32:00-07:00","id":848836,"title":"","content":"This is really helpful, folks. Keep it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:09:02-07:00","id":848884,"title":"","content":"How weird do you want to get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:47:20-07:00","id":848961,"title":"","content":"One thing that would be helpful in the player's guide is a short section or table that summarizes general Beast abilities. It's hard enough to describe Beast as a concept to new players (even CofD players) but an appendix or something that keeps that information readily available would be very helpful. For example, traversing the Primordial Pathways, Mother's Kiss, Family Resemblence, Family Dinner, imposing lair traits, anything that all beasts can DO in short summary on one page would be great to have around (sort of like an expanded screen I guess). Just the name, the roll, the cost (if any), and a one sentence summary.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree with what's been posted so far. The most important aspect of the Player's Guide should be helping players have a deeper understanding of what it means to be a beast. I want more information on what different beasts go through in their daily lives, how they interact with each other, how they interact with their mortal families. Most of this is covered in the core but a greater amount of detail will be valuable to players who want that extra layer of depth. Perhaps exploring further the concept of a beast being torn between their mortal family and their brood. One of the highlights of beast is that dichotomy of mortal life and monster life.<br /> <br /> Also, I love what ArcaneArts said about good and evil. Many players have a very black and white concept of being a monster. Let's explore the grey area! Beasts are the stuff of nightmares and fear but that doesn't make them innately evil. A section on this concept could help players understand that it isn't so simple as 'you're a spooky villain'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4716-shredgasm","name":"shredgasm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T20:43:04-07:00","id":849112,"title":"","content":"I will definitely agree with those asking for a more in-depth look at a Beast's lair. <br /> <br /> The other biggie for me would be a look at how a Beast interacts with dreams in more detail. Can she feed by going into someone's dream and inducing nightmares like her Horror does? How does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T22:24:02-07:00","id":849147,"title":"","content":"A look at uses for the standard delay option on Nightmares besides subliminal Social Maneuvering \u2014 a lot of the mechanical effects of any given Nightmare just aren't of much use on a sleeping target and they all have the same secondary effect, so why use one Presence-based Nightmare over another when you're queuing up the line of horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T23:02:02-07:00","id":849159,"title":"","content":"Things I'd like to see:<ul><li>A list of Horror inspirations, both historical and modern, and possible Family concepts for them.</li> <li>Minions, both in the waking world and in the Lair. If the Beast brings a Werewolf into his Gloomy Forest Chamber, would the Werewolf be able to interact in any kind of meaningful way with the pack of wolves that provide that sweet music of the night, or are they just wolf shaped sound effect generators?</li> <li>More on Lairs and Burrows, especially some &quot;In character&quot; perspectives on what Chambers look and feel like to Beasts and non-Beasts alike. Also some expansion of how Beasts can modify a Chamber's appearance and/or nature, either when they add the Chamber or as they gain more Lair traits.</li> <li>More Atavisms and Kinship Nightmares.</li> <li>A section on how Beasts perceive and interact with the world around them, given the advantages they can gain from Environmental Immunity. An example would be an Eshmaki that has Darkness as a Lair trait, so she can see in the dark. Does she even notice when the lights go out suddenly, or would she just keep on reading her book?</li> <li>Examples of Satiety potentials, especially things that a High-Satiety Beast would find acceptable to his Horror.</li> <li>A &quot;Day in the Life&quot; section for a Brood. How they would hunt together (or apart), how they would interact with their Kin, and how they would team up to deal with a Hero entering a Broodmember's Lair; would all be interesting concepts to explore.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9032-lurkbeast","name":"LurkBeast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9032_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T02:38:56-07:00","id":849185,"title":"","content":"Extra Stories And Lives for the Families and Hungers would be great :&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:41:07-07:00","id":849221,"title":"","content":"A sentence on how being over 5 dots in lair affects your aging would be nice. e.g. after reading that a changeling gets younger, I realized I hadn't seen what happens for a Beast when they do that. I had just assumed beasts aged slowly, but most of them didn't survive long enough for it to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:28:43-07:00","id":849244,"title":"","content":"Some material on how Beasts might try to manage their Hungers in keeping with their formerly human moral codes, or some sort of moral code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:37:35-07:00","id":849251,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think Beast is busy enough without the Breaking Point mechanic. Not having them provides a broad continuum of grays for the Children to exist in. Although I could see it as some kind of Anathema imposed upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:31:01-07:00","id":849364,"title":"","content":"More options for &quot;Empathetic&quot; heroes, if only to make things more tragic when the final curtain calls. Lots of potential for drama and powerful scenes of emotion between a Beast and his would-be slayer. Especially if they're in love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:36:32-07:00","id":849368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849364#post849364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More options for &amp;quot;Empathetic&amp;quot; heroes, if only to make things more tragic when the final curtain calls. Lots of potential for drama and powerful scenes of emotion between a Beast and his would-be slayer. Especially if they're in love.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this sounds more like something for the Storyteller book, but an exploration of how Beasts relate to Heroes from the player's side would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:11:29-07:00","id":849384,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Lair, which has been brought up several times, an alterntive system comes to mind-one where you have a few lair traits imposed by the Beast's nature themselves, but makes it so that each Chamber you create comes with it's own set of tags, to help make more individually more distinctive rooms. The increase of access to Lair as an imposition that comes with Chambers is cool, but I found the risk that the mechanical sameness of Chambers undercuts the importance of seeking out new set pieces.<br /> <br /> Only related in a tiny way, a Beast Playlist on Onyx Path's youtube channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:28:00-07:00","id":849391,"title":"","content":"I think something could be done with the idea that each Chamber has an story that invading Heroes naturally want to complete, even if it's as simple as scaling the cliff, swimming across the river, or finding the secret entrance (passage to another chamber)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:50:57-07:00","id":849487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849251#post849251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think Beast is busy enough without the Breaking Point mechanic. Not having them provides a broad continuum of grays for the Children to exist in. Although I could see it as some kind of Anathema imposed upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that SunlessNick was asking for breaking points. I think the intent was for Beasts that feed their Hunger without seeming like the 'bad guys'. I know my wife has had a hard time getting into the game because she doesn't like playing evil characters, and she has had difficulty seeing them as anything else. The best she's been able to give it so far is to think that while they have to do horrible things, they can choose to do them to horrible people. I'm sure that she'd love some more examples of Beasts that seem like they're a positive influence on the world.<br /> <br /> As for what I'd like to see, I think some more details on Hungers would be great. For instance, if a Beast with the Hunger for the Hoard steals an expensive diamond necklace, do they get the Satiety at once, or do they get it at the moment the owner realizes it? If the latter, would they need to be present for it, or would they suddenly feel their Satiety increase at some random point in the future? Can they gain it even if the person doesn't realize the item is gone, such as a talented art thief stealing a valuable painting but replacing it with a forgery? I would love to see questions like that answered. I also wouldn't mind seeing a new Hunger or two show up.<br /> <br /> I would like to see Lair traits addressed in more depth, especially for ones that are a little less intuitive. For instance, what does it mean for a Beast to be immune to Sealed Exits?<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Kinship Nightmares contrasted with regular ones, possibly with some thought of how a Beast may gain appropriate Nightmares without the usual Kin. For example, a Beast with a Hunger that drives him to disorient people who has the Maze trait seems like a character that could quite reasonably develop the You Are Lost Nightmare, even if he doesn't know any changelings.<br /> <br /> I share the desire of several others to see minions and other resident creatures of the Beast's Lair, even if it was as simple as n Inhabited Lair trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:54:40-07:00","id":849490,"title":"","content":"seeing all the great suggestions that make more sense for the ST book, can we have that first? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> not a serious suggestion, though on the serious note, why don't the ST guides come out first, no ST no game... ST needs more material. (sorry that this entire statement is rather derailing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T16:02:24-07:00","id":849494,"title":"","content":"I think strictly feeding on horrible people misses a whole dimension of the game.<br /> <br /> A family that was losing their appreciation of one another finds new reasons to love and trust each other in the face of a Ruin, not knowing the Beast did it to help.<br /> <br /> An aspiring artist is blocked from the higher rungs of the film society by the Power of the judge, the Beast knowing that the artist will benefit from time and desperation in producing greater works.<br /> <br /> A woman is caught, Prey to an incomprehensible monster, the smoke in her lungs and drugs in her blood slowing her down. The next day, she has some new scars, but more importantly she understands now what some of the consequences of her abuse of substances is doing to her.<br /> <br /> Horrible people can suffer, but good and decent people can become epics when a Beast decides to tear out the dross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T16:12:33-07:00","id":849498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849494#post849494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think strictly feeding on horrible people misses a whole dimension of the game.<br /> <br /> A family that was losing their appreciation of one another finds new reasons to love and trust each other in the face of a Ruin, not knowing the Beast did it to help.<br /> <br /> An aspiring artist is blocked from the higher rungs of the film society by the Power of the judge, the Beast knowing that the artist will benefit from time and desperation in producing greater works.<br /> <br /> A woman is caught, Prey to an incomprehensible monster, the smoke in her lungs and drugs in her blood slowing her down. The next day, she has some new scars, but more importantly she understands now what some of the consequences of her abuse of substances is doing to her.<br /> <br /> Horrible people can suffer, but good and decent people can become epics when a Beast decides to tear out the dross.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, when I say I want more information on how use nightmares to teach lessons, I want more on stuff like this. I feel like the core book is a little unclear how you can use the nightmares effectively (since some beasts teach poorly). How does the beast find out, and go on about taking action to improve or tear down the lives of people. How does it ensure that its nightmares have the desired effect, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T16:14:35-07:00","id":849499,"title":"","content":"I think it'll be fair to say that there will be more of this in the Player's Guide. It's an integral part of the Hungers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:00:20-07:00","id":849510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849494#post849494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think strictly feeding on horrible people misses a whole dimension of the game.<br /> <br /> A family that was losing their appreciation of one another finds new reasons to love and trust each other in the face of a Ruin, not knowing the Beast did it to help.<br /> <br /> An aspiring artist is blocked from the higher rungs of the film society by the Power of the judge, the Beast knowing that the artist will benefit from time and desperation in producing greater works.<br /> <br /> A woman is caught, Prey to an incomprehensible monster, the smoke in her lungs and drugs in her blood slowing her down. The next day, she has some new scars, but more importantly she understands now what some of the consequences of her abuse of substances is doing to her.<br /> <br /> Horrible people can suffer, but good and decent people can become epics when a Beast decides to tear out the dross.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what I'd really like to see. What happens when the Beast gets it wrong. What happens when the family choose a scapegoat to blame the Ruin upon and the relationship breaks forever, or when the aspiring artist spirals into depression and suicide.<br /> <br /> That's where the real stories are. Once the Beast's scared the woman away from substance abuse there's rarely anything left to do, but struggling to fix your mistake can be a nice long story.<br /> <br /> Besides, you know it's going to happen all the time. Beasts don't have a &quot;identify appropriate student&quot; or &quot;write perfect lesson plans&quot; Atavisms. There's a reason why in the real world of therapy is no therapy without the patients consent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-18-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:03:53-07:00","id":849513,"title":"","content":"So, basically, when Heroes are born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T01:37:10-07:00","id":849648,"title":"","content":"Not at all.<br /> <br /> The standard Beast-Hero story is one where the two battle to the death. Life and death battles have an inherent way of grabbing the dramatic spotlight, if a Beast tries to bring a family together and breaks it apart I want the Beast to deal with that consequence directly; rather than substitute it for a different combat heavy conflict.<br /> <br /> In addition thematically you're between Scylla and Charybdis. If turning into a Hero makes the mortal into a significantly worse person as it typically does then the thematics become dangerously close to victim blaming - yes the Beast ruined her life, but she's in the wrong for not forgiving the Beast. (It may have been an accident on the Beast's part, but when you play with fire you can't just claim it's an accident when something gets burnt.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand if she becomes genuinely Heroic and a better person because of it then it's another story about a Beast tearing out the dross. Which is of course a perfectly appropriate story, for example: Batman's origin, but it is an example of a Beast's lesson going right (for a certain definition of right) and doesn't fill the niche about a Beast's lessons going wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:32:39-07:00","id":849730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849487#post849487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that SunlessNick was asking for breaking points. I think the intent was for Beasts that feed their Hunger without seeming like the 'bad guys'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. I don't care about breaking points, but there will be Beasts whose previous human lives and mores and connections haven't become meaningless to them, so some discussion of how they might try to exist within those bounds (maybe broken down by Lives) would I think be a worthwhile addition. If for no other reason that the number of people who find it hard to see how they can even attempt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:42:01-07:00","id":849737,"title":"","content":"Technically speaking, a Hero isn't necessarily turned into a Beast-hunting obsessive. They need to be Integrity 4 or lower to become obsessed with hunting Beasts, and with the egotistical ideas of the Monomyth protagonist. Before that, a Hero is a person who can sense disturbances in the Primordial Dream, a person who can feel fear as a palpable force. They are predisposed to look for Beasts, since Beasts share a similar intrinsic connection to the Primordial Dream, but that doesn't stop them from looking for the true source of the fear and trying to address it.<br /> <br /> Taking your 'failed Lesson' examples from the last page, let's throw an Integrity 5+ Hero into the mix.<br /> <br /> The Hero finds the scapegoat and works to restore the family relationship, and find what was the source of the family's fears that made them project them onto the scapegoat.<br /> <br /> The Hero tracks down the artist and acts as their rock, helping them struggle with their depression.<br /> <br /> The Hero tracks down the scarred addict and tries to help them get clean.<br /> <br /> This is what I think Heroes did before everything went wrong. The Beast introduced the Lesson, but it was the Hero who drew the information from it, it was the Hero who helped dredge wisdom from primal panic. The Hero would help the person consumed by fear overcome it, and in doing so learn something themselves- a Lesson they could take and carry with them, without the need for the primordial fear. Basically, the Hero would put others before themselves, and genuinely try to help them. This isn't to say a High-Integrity Hero won't hunt Beasts. If the Beast goes too far, if they become a menace rather than just problematic, then the Hero steps in and defeats the monster at their door. The Low-Integrity Hero doesn't care about the victims, they think it's all about them. They refuse to learn anything, and the kill becomes everything to them. The glory of hunting down the monster and killing it.<br /> <br /> I think a High-Integrity Hero can be a real force for good, but I'm also of the opinion that a High-Integrity Hero isn't likely to go looking for Beasts, or other supernatural creatures, and instead tackles other sources of fear. All they know is that they don't like seeing people afraid, and that they want to help. A High-Integrity Hero who accidentally stumbles across a Beast in the course of the Hero's career as a psychotherapist would be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:37:52-07:00","id":849842,"title":"","content":"So flippancy asides, the big problem for Beast right now is that people have an overt obsession on the brutal nature of Beasts and the incorrect assumption that there are only so many correct ways to feed. I have seen &quot;The only responsible way to eat is to hunt horrible people&quot; too many times to count, and &quot;Man, I'd like to see how Beast's attempt to better people's lives while handling their brutal nature results in abject failure&quot; exactly once.<br /> <br /> It's clear to me which of these is actually a problem to address.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:42:26-07:00","id":849905,"title":"","content":"Am I really the only person who asked about what happens when Beasts lessons go horribly wrong? I would have thought that is an exceptionally obvious question to ask.<br /> <br /> That said, I do have a lot of sympathy for the people who think the only responsible way to eat is to hunt horrible people; and even then my natural instinct is to respond two ways don't make a right. I did mean what I said about the importance of consent in the last page. Even if it does all work out for the better, it's still immoral if you don't get consent first, and if I'm honest I'd give it 50/50 whether you'd find a Beast teaching racists to be tolerant or teaching tolerant people to be racist. Where does racism come from if not the darkest and most primordial parts of the human psyche?<br /> <br /> But I agree with you about what's actually a problem to address. Firstly Beast is now published, and I doubt anyone would want to rewrite it a third time even if it wasn't. Secondly like most WoD games it's about playing monsters. Vampire would be pretty boring if everyone used the immortality to set up compound interest schemes, only brought blood with money, and spent their time doing something more ethical than backstabbing each other in an eternal dense of treacherous politics. Beast would be boring if everyone taught lessons by becoming a licensed therapist and paying strict attention to professional ethics while avoiding any feeding save Family Dinner via watching Werewolves hunting wild deer for dinner.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast is what Beast is. If you don't think Beasts feeding is moral, tell stories about immoral Beasts. They're supposed to be monsters, or use them as antagonists for Hunter (to be fair, that's what I do. I think my Beast opposed Compact is possibly my best).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:25:27-07:00","id":849924,"title":"","content":"Somehow, I think you've assumed that a call of attention to the culture of Beasts means we're somehow going to forget that Beasts are monsters.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":".  I can be nice. 03-19-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T00:50:17-07:00","id":850051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848571#post848571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not about evil. It's about being a monster.<br /> <br /> Because, unlike Becoming Nightmare, the Inheritances are much more emotionally complex for any given Beast. To Thine Own Self Be True is challenged by the Inheritances, which ask questions about just what is the self of a Beast.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, the villain isn't the villain.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, even if the villain is the villain, it's a better choice than giving up who you are.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, your choices are inevitable, and your destiny is never certain.<br /> <br /> Because, sometimes, a tragedy is the sort of story you want to live, because the alternatives as emptier still.<br /> <br /> Because all the love and kindness in the world doesn't do a damn thing if a person isn't willing to move and change themselves.<br /> <br /> Because the Inheritances aren't the only endgames you have.<br /> <br /> In short, because Beast is more complicated than most people seem to get. Cough.<br /> <br /> A fuller response is coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't fully caught up with this thread, but I find myself agreeing here. Beast as a game isn't more than just being a monster, being the hero of the story, or just being plain suicidal. Beast: The Primordial is a game of choices and consequences, of lessons and personal identity. In a way, it's a story about life. And the daily problems it brings.<br /> <br /> Moving onto expectations, having a more in depth look into the Beast psyche, as well as some new Atavisms and Nightmares. Though admittedly, with all the homebrew on those two power sets, that's not a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T00:55:12-07:00","id":850053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849737#post849737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically speaking, a Hero isn't necessarily turned into a Beast-hunting obsessive. They need to be Integrity 4 or lower to become obsessed with hunting Beasts, and with the egotistical ideas of the Monomyth protagonist. Before that, a Hero is a person who can sense disturbances in the Primordial Dream, a person who can feel fear as a palpable force. They are predisposed to look for Beasts, since Beasts share a similar intrinsic connection to the Primordial Dream, but that doesn't stop them from looking for the true source of the fear and trying to address it.<br /> <br /> Taking your 'failed Lesson' examples from the last page, let's throw an Integrity 5+ Hero into the mix.<br /> <br /> The Hero finds the scapegoat and works to restore the family relationship, and find what was the source of the family's fears that made them project them onto the scapegoat.<br /> <br /> The Hero tracks down the artist and acts as their rock, helping them struggle with their depression.<br /> <br /> The Hero tracks down the scarred addict and tries to help them get clean.<br /> <br /> This is what I think Heroes did before everything went wrong. The Beast introduced the Lesson, but it was the Hero who drew the information from it, it was the Hero who helped dredge wisdom from primal panic. The Hero would help the person consumed by fear overcome it, and in doing so learn something themselves- a Lesson they could take and carry with them, without the need for the primordial fear. Basically, the Hero would put others before themselves, and genuinely try to help them. This isn't to say a High-Integrity Hero won't hunt Beasts. If the Beast goes too far, if they become a menace rather than just problematic, then the Hero steps in and defeats the monster at their door. The Low-Integrity Hero doesn't care about the victims, they think it's all about them. They refuse to learn anything, and the kill becomes everything to them. The glory of hunting down the monster and killing it.<br /> <br /> I think a High-Integrity Hero can be a real force for good, but I'm also of the opinion that a High-Integrity Hero isn't likely to go looking for Beasts, or other supernatural creatures, and instead tackles other sources of fear. All they know is that they don't like seeing people afraid, and that they want to help. A High-Integrity Hero who accidentally stumbles across a Beast in the course of the Hero's career as a psychotherapist would be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's another thing I'd like to see in the future. A sidebar section (or even a full supplement) that deals in playing the Hero as...well, a hero. And the high Integrity Heroes at that. Until then, though, homebrewing the mechanics shouldn't be too hard.... In fact, the Extraordinary Mortal and Dark Hero templates from Mirrors could offer some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T02:35:29-07:00","id":850066,"title":"","content":"Has Matt changed his policy on &quot;no playable heroes ever?&quot; If he hasn't might I recomend Princess? Princesses and Beasts make brilliant antagonists for each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849924#post849924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow, I think you've assumed that a call of attention to the culture of Beasts means we're somehow going to forget that Beasts are monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I got that assumption from the way you talk about feeding, particularly on the previous page.<br /> <br /> White Oak Dragon asked for ways to play Beast without being evil. You responded with a list of ways to feed which while cool and thematic, were all rather evil. Your last line in particular.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849494#post849494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horrible people can suffer, but good and decent people can become epics when a Beast decides to tear out the dross.</div> </div> </div> </div>makes it sound like you think the aforementioned feeding was a good thing to do. It's not. It makes a good story, but without consent it's a monstrous and evil thing to do.<br /> <br /> You've already said you think this impression is wrong, but I thought you'd like to know where it comes from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:27:10-07:00","id":850130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=849905#post849905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I really the only person who asked about what happens when Beasts lessons go horribly wrong? I would have thought that is an exceptionally obvious question to ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more suitable for the ST Guide.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:57:04-07:00","id":850142,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd really like to see is an expanded look at the lessons that Beasts teach, and how they affect both the Beasts and their &quot;students.&quot; I'd like to see Beasts that manage to teach their lessons effectively gain something from doing so, even if it was something as simple as regaining Willpower. I'd like to see some support for Horrors that actually do care about the lesson, rather than all Horrors being animalistic eating machines. I'd like the lessons to seem like they truly matter, instead of seeming like they're just a Beast's rationalization for why they feed their inner monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:11:26-07:00","id":850143,"title":"","content":"Honestly, lessons always felt like something tacked on at the very end in kneejerk response to the complaints about the power fantasy aspect of the game. We don't know much about them and Satiety isn't a good fit for hanging some &quot;morality&quot; mechanic that manages lessons onto it.<br /> <br /> IMO, this isn't a big issue. Beasts shouldn't have some morality code. They have to get that from their human side (i.e., it can come from their concept). This makes worked examples of lessons indispensable to both PG and STG. Examples of lessons going right and wrong should be in both books.<br /> <br /> Good and evil aren't really a factor though. People are just projecting their preconceived notions of what each is. In Beast, much like in real life, what is actually good or evil isn't as clear cut. <br /> <br /> It's important to get out of your comfort zone and remember that from the ancient Aztecs perspective, sacrificing your enemy's heart is objectively good. It ensures that the rains will come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 03-20-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T13:57:35-07:00","id":850244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850066#post850066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has Matt changed his policy on &quot;no playable heroes ever?&quot; If he hasn't might I recomend Princess? Princesses and Beasts make brilliant antagonists for each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually I got that assumption from the way you talk about feeding, particularly on the previous page.<br /> <br /> White Oak Dragon asked for ways to play Beast without being evil. You responded with a list of ways to feed which while cool and thematic, were all rather evil. Your last line in particular.makes it sound like you think the aforementioned feeding was a good thing to do. It's not. It makes a good story, but without consent it's a monstrous and evil thing to do.<br /> <br /> You've already said you think this impression is wrong, but I thought you'd like to know where it comes from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was going ot respond in here, and then I realized there's derailing going on. So <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/850242-beast-nature-and-morality\">I made another thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T18:32:49-07:00","id":850354,"title":"","content":"The core mentions briefly that Hungers can change, I'd like to know more about Beasts who push themselves toward an acquired taste.<br /> Like, what happens if you manage to establish yourself as a local legend but in a way that doesn't quite mesh with your Hunger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:54:14-07:00","id":850636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850143#post850143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, lessons always felt like something tacked on at the very end in kneejerk response to the complaints about the power fantasy aspect of the game. We don't know much about them and Satiety isn't a good fit for hanging some &quot;morality&quot; mechanic that manages lessons onto it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> However, I also don't think that the idea of &quot;Teaching&quot; is particularly bad. I would like to see more ambiguity about this purpose and show Beasts who follow that philosophy and what they do, but also Beasts who disagree with the philosophy and have their own philosophies as to what Beasts should be doing. Some variety here would better flesh out what culture Beasts have and disagreements are key to stirring up drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely want to see more options presented in the Player's Guide, and not just one philosophy that's presented as an objective truth. Chronicles of Darkness have always had mystery and uncertainty to purpose and I'd really like to see more of that presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:15:40-07:00","id":850651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850636#post850636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> However, I also don't think that the idea of &amp;quot;Teaching&amp;quot; is particularly bad. I would like to see more ambiguity about this purpose and show Beasts who follow that philosophy and what they do, but also Beasts who disagree with the philosophy and have their own philosophies as to what Beasts should be doing. Some variety here would better flesh out what culture Beasts have and disagreements are key to stirring up drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely want to see more options presented in the Player's Guide, and not just one philosophy that's presented as an objective truth. Chronicles of Darkness have always had mystery and uncertainty to purpose and I'd really like to see more of that presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, yes! The teaching aspect is an inspired idea, but I want to see more variations at how Beasts look at the world. I like that Beasts can start shit for the greater good, but that is a very dangerous road to walk. I want options for Beasts who refuse to walk it too, for both altruistic and selfish reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:45:58-07:00","id":850670,"title":"","content":"I would like more atavisms as well as a system on making atvatisms could be fun also more merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:20:14-07:00","id":850700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850636#post850636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> However, I also don't think that the idea of &quot;Teaching&quot; is particularly bad. I would like to see more ambiguity about this purpose and show Beasts who follow that philosophy and what they do, but also Beasts who disagree with the philosophy and have their own philosophies as to what Beasts should be doing. Some variety here would better flesh out what culture Beasts have and disagreements are key to stirring up drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely want to see more options presented in the Player's Guide, and not just one philosophy that's presented as an objective truth. Chronicles of Darkness have always had mystery and uncertainty to purpose and I'd really like to see more of that presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this note I'd like to link a thread from rpg.net, containing some sample faction and ideologies:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?769133-Beast-The-Big-Analysis-Thread&amp;p=19519294#post19519294\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...4#post19519294</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?769133-Beast-The-Big-Analysis-Thread&amp;p=19519952#post19519952\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...2#post19519952</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?769133-Beast-The-Big-Analysis-Thread&amp;p=19520390#post19520390\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...0#post19520390</a><br /> <br /> A greater variety of ideologies would perfectly underscore &quot;no neat boxes&quot; premise. If you could create a modular system to build some, that would have been amazing.<br /> <br /> Also, shamelessly steal from &quot;Circle of the Crone&quot; Covenant Book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T12:02:42-07:00","id":850731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850636#post850636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I also don't think that the idea of &quot;Teaching&quot; is particularly bad. I would like to see more ambiguity about this purpose and show Beasts who follow that philosophy and what they do, but also Beasts who disagree with the philosophy and have their own philosophies as to what Beasts should be doing. Some variety here would better flesh out what culture Beasts have and disagreements are key to stirring up drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely want to see more options presented in the Player's Guide, and not just one philosophy that's presented as an objective truth. Chronicles of Darkness have always had mystery and uncertainty to purpose and I'd really like to see more of that presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like this too. Essentially, philosophical splats, even if they're not referred to in such a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T16:33:51-07:00","id":850849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850636#post850636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> However, I also don't think that the idea of &quot;Teaching&quot; is particularly bad. I would like to see more ambiguity about this purpose and show Beasts who follow that philosophy and what they do, but also Beasts who disagree with the philosophy and have their own philosophies as to what Beasts should be doing. Some variety here would better flesh out what culture Beasts have and disagreements are key to stirring up drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely want to see more options presented in the Player's Guide, and not just one philosophy that's presented as an objective truth. Chronicles of Darkness have always had mystery and uncertainty to purpose and I'd really like to see more of that presented.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=850731#post850731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like this too. Essentially, philosophical splats, even if they're not referred to in such a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crap, the forum ate my rather long post. Let's see if I can make it shorter this time.<br /> <br /> More information on how different Beasts view feeding and teaching lessons would be nice. It wouldn't have to be anything big, but if it were to be more heavily expanded on something similar to Agendas from Demon would be welcome. On a social level it would be nice to have a section on what it's like for a Beast attempting to be a part of vampire society and what it's like to be a member of a pack of werewolves and other stuff like that. Similar to this, I'd also like information on Beasts interacting with stranger stuff like spirits and really rare monsters that aren't usually playable.<br /> <br /> Expanding on Kinship and Lairs, I'd like more information on how Kinship changes a Lair. The section in the book that talked about how having Kinship with a Sin-Eater can sometimes create an Avernian Gate was really cool to me and I'd like more information on it and similar things. A merit that could represent having such a thing in your Lair would be cool, but isn't necessary if we could get enough information about it. I'd also like information on what it's like and what benefits and drawbacks can be gained by letting ghosts, spirits, and other monsters live in your Lair as guardians and friends. A merit that would allow ghosts to treat you as an anchor or something similar could be pretty cool for helping facilitate this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> As far as merits go, I'd like information on how to use Retainer to represent ephemeral beings and other monsters or a merit that could help represent something like that. I would also absolutely love merits that would make your Horror stronger in some way, be it by adding more points to split between Power, Finesse, Resistance, and Size, or something else entirely. Speaking of Horrors, I'm kind of interested in how increasing its size is useful seeing as how size doesn't add to health. It kind of makes having a huge horror a liability because every point you put into size could be put into something else instead. Merits that could alter your Lair in some way would be really nice too, especially if it was something like that idea for an Avernian Gate merit I mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to know what other worlds like the Shadow, Hedge, and Astral are like for Beasts along with more information on the Primordial Dream, but I can understand if that's more of a Storyteller's Guide thing.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I'm really looking forward to the Player's Guide and the Storyteller's Guide when that finally starts getting written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T21:47:26-07:00","id":850961,"title":"","content":"Maybe something on the beasts opinions of the Dark Mother, and their Symbiotic? relationship with their Horror. Also possibly stuff on what the horror is doing in the primordial if it survive's its Beast. I'm especially curious if perhaps the Horror finds a child in the dream to attach to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T01:24:21-07:00","id":851019,"title":"","content":"Something else that came to me yesterday - I'd like to see more about how and why Beasts interact with the other worlds not directly related to them: the Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:09:42-07:00","id":852920,"title":"","content":"How about a power that allows the Beast to swallow a target whole (like the wolf from Little Red Riding Hood, or the whale from Pinocchio)--which lands said-target in the Beast's lair until &quot;released&quot; or they somehow escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:13:59-07:00","id":852922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=852920#post852920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a power that allows the Beast to swallow a target whole (like the wolf from Little Red Riding Hood, or the whale from Pinocchio)--which lands said-target in the Beast's lair until &quot;released&quot; or they somehow escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have a go at making that an Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:33:16-07:00","id":854729,"title":"","content":"I want to know about Beasts who don't want to teach lessons, or who don't believe or perhaps are anti Dark Mother","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:52:06-07:00","id":854737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=854729#post854729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to know about Beasts who don't want to teach lessons, or who don't believe or perhaps are anti Dark Mother</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a lot to know about a negative and hunting the ur-cryptid because you mean her harm isn't really meaningfully different in practice from making that pursuit for more benign reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:05:25-07:00","id":854739,"title":"","content":"On Beast's wanting not wanting to teach lessons, It's worth noting (again) that Horrors don't give a shit about the lessons. The culture of teaching is a buy in, an answer to the question any Beast might come to after gorging themselves on the people around for the hundredth time and asking &quot;Fuck, is there anymore to life than this?&quot; Kind of like how vampires eventually asking if they're anymore than a walking rape metaphor. It can be expected that in any discussion of the Families or the Hungers, other things are going to be looked at. The cultural answer of filling in for the Heroes as is just a predominant answer, not an all consuming imperative. And honestly, yes, you can blame the teaching culture very equally on the Heroes as much as existential musings.<br /> <br /> As for disbelief or anti-Dark Mother, that's one's a little harder to pull off, particularly since the fiction points at Mama Crow being more involved with her kids than previously thought, and a decently sized potion of this thread asks for ways for Beasts to interact with it. Still, It's worth noting that that aside, the Dark Mother is something, at this point, that's like the Atlantis mythos of Mage-a convienent fill in that explains the metaphysics of Beasts. Certainly, there's room to explore a few blasphemies.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I find that boring. There's more fun to be had saying &quot;This Bitch-Goddess is Here to Rock&quot; than to spend too much time with Beasts going all academic on us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:42:43-07:00","id":854751,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what should be done with the fact that a beast's 'soul' is, in actually, a conglomerate symbol of people en masse and that therefore every Beast contains multitudes/every individual Beast is a cacophanic racket as a chorus of screams long held, but something should be done with the fact that the Horror is not an icon for a singular identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:59:33-07:00","id":854954,"title":"","content":"Reading through the thread, I see several ideas I'd like to see expanded on, either here or in the Storyteller's Guide. Off-hand, I'd like to see material on:<br /> <br /> <i>* The Care and Feeding of Princesses</i> - From Hansel &amp; Gretel to high fantasy epics, many Beasts seem to have an interest in keeping a long-term &quot;guest&quot;. After all, what self-respecting dragon doesn't have their own princess? Sure, in the modern day they might have to settle for an heiress, govt. official's daughter, or movie star, but its the principle that counts!<br /> <br /> Exploring the phenomena could be interesting. Sure, it could be an outgrowth of the &quot;Lessons&quot; idea (what better way to teach a snobby rich kid to appreciate their wealth and servants, than by making them scrub the floors themselves), but are there other reasons? Are they <i>de facto</i> familiars? Are they a status symbol? Do Beasts in a Hive compete to have the most famous/exotic/cool &quot;princess&quot;?<br /> <br /> And what happens when a mage, interested in learning more about Beasts, <i>volunteers</i> for the position?<br /> <br /> * <i>Public Awareness</i> - Given that Beasts need humanity to react to them, in order to feed, it makes sense that they'd have some sort of &quot;Reputation&quot; or &quot;Public Awareness&quot; score. At what point do rumors start to spread? Or conspiracy forums or &quot;news of the weird&quot; articles start focusing on a Beast's hunts? When does my character get their own underground comic, and what does it take to get your own police task force hunting you?<br /> <br /> * <i>Social Impact</i> - Similar to &quot;Public Awareness&quot;, what effects does a Beast have on the society around them? If a Nemesis (with a Hunger for Punishment) decides to go all Batman on the local criminals, how fast do the rumors spread? At what point do they start to make a noticeable impact on the crime levels? What tactics will the local mob (and vampires) start taking to preserve their turf?<br /> <br /> The other Hungers would presumably have their own impacts - a Beast into Ruin, and a flair of explosives, will have a very noticeable one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . But what about the Collector who specializes in rare art/books/artifacts? At some point, (human) collectors (and probably mages) would start getting interested in their collection. . .<br /> <br /> * <i>Expanded Info on Lairs</i> - Personally, I'd like a &quot;Scaling&quot; or &quot;Giant Size&quot; Lair trait, to help &quot;big&quot; monsters come across as suitably impressive. That way your Anakim could throw a prisoner in a giant bird cage, while the tiny Hero hides in a mouse hole, looking for a moment to strike.<br /> <br /> I'm also not clear on whether Beasts can add chambers with supernatural properties. For example, can a Beast visiting Tokyo annex an &quot;ansho&quot; (mana draining zone)? What about the Fountain of Youth (or Well of Madness)? If a PC stumbles across the &quot;Library of Skulls&quot;, where the severed heads of the dead must answer any question truthfully, can add they add it to their Lair? And if so, do the original properties transfer properly, or are they twisted by the Lair?<br /> <br /> Some sample Lairs and unique chambers might be nice, too. Inspiration for new players, on how to make their own Lairs suitably freaky.<br /> <br /> * However, one thing I'm not interested in (at least for the Player's Guide) is information on playable Heroes. Unless things have changed, the corebook was pretty clear that Beasts don't really run into the more stable ones - only the crazies that have gotten obsessed with hunting them. I'm not 100% clear on whether the average Beast even knows that Heroes come in non-&quot;murderous wacko&quot; flavors. At some point, a Hero spinoff supplement might make sense, but in the Player's Guide I'd prefer the focus to be on Heroes as antagonists (&quot;101 Ways to Hero-Proof Your Lair <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><i>Edit</i></u>: Oh, and good luck, Matt! You came up with a cool game line, and I can't wait to see what comes next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 03-29-2016, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:57:28-07:00","id":854973,"title":"","content":"Huh, the Princess idea is kind of neat. Perhaps it would make for a good mortal template. Well done One Vorlon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:10:52-07:00","id":854980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=854973#post854973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, the Princess idea is kind of neat. Perhaps it would make for a good mortal template. Well done One Vorlon!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It reminds me of the stuff in Dragon: The Embers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:14:17-07:00","id":855107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=854954#post854954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, in the modern day they might have to settle for an heiress, govt. official's daughter, or movie star, but its the principle that counts!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you know, bunch of countries in Europe, Middle-East and Asia (I am not sure about Africa) still does have monarchies with princesses included.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T11:41:14-07:00","id":855150,"title":"","content":"Actually, the idea of the princess, taking someone and making them a familiar, is rife with a lot of cool ideas.<br /> <br /> The rest of Vorlon's post is pretty cool, but that's the one that has my ears perked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:08:43-07:00","id":855201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=848370#post848370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's sort of what I was thinking too. Minions as a Lair trait. That said, it could be something more oriented to player characters too, but you're quite right that Kinship fills the function pretty well in the abstract.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:26:39-07:00","id":855241,"title":"","content":"I have only quickly read the previous posts, so my suggestions may be redundant, but here they are:<br /> <br /> -Rules for creating new Atavisms, and the possibility of new Atavisms being inspired by other monsters, like Nightmares.<br /> -More examples of feeding and lessons.<br /> -More feeding options: Options to feed on symbolism and/or narrative significance as well as emotion; or feeding on awe as well as fear.<br /> -An equivalent to Vampires' bloodlines or Changelings' entitlements. Archetypes?<br /> -Options encouraging less directly predatory contacts with mortals: perhaps a way to become the guardian/protector/symbol of a territory or community, in a mystically significant way.<br /> -Treasure or trophies. Specifically, objects/body parts created/owned by Beasts that other creatures might covet, like a naga's pearl, a vouivre's escarboucle, a kitsune's ball, an unicorn's horn...<br /> -More exploration of non-atagonistic relationships between both Broods and individual Beasts.<br /> -Beast organizations/societies; Cults of the Dark Mother, monster creating corporations, etc...<br /> -More info on the Primordial Dream and whatever (or whoever) can be found there.<br /> -More Lair customization options.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:50:47-07:00","id":855971,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can think of right off-hand that my group really wants to see is an ability to assume monstrous form. Bonus points if it's customizable like a demon or similar. That gives us a big set of options for &quot;monstrous shapeshifter&quot; types, which would be great for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T01:24:45-07:00","id":856337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=855971#post855971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I can think of right off-hand that my group really wants to see is an ability to assume monstrous form. Bonus points if it's customizable like a demon or similar. That gives us a big set of options for &quot;monstrous shapeshifter&quot; types, which would be great for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this one. I see one of the strengths of Beast as the fact that they don't have a monstrous form. (And looking at some dev comments from Dark Eras, never did.) They're creatures of nightmare, they inhabit the deepest fears of your darkest nights, they linger in half-imagined forms and bring their power through in (mostly) unseen ways that terrify the victim in what they didn't see, not what they did. Victims can't rationalise what happens because they can't see anything. Their mind fills in the gaps from the dark places or irrational fear.<br /> <br /> If Beasts had a 'monstrous shapeshifter' form, that would be the antithesis of Beast's elegance, dilute their fear, and just lead to a blunt 'monster' splat, not a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T01:44:52-07:00","id":856341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=856337#post856337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and just lead to a blunt 'monster' splat, not a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I accept most of your points as preferences, but this one I think is untrue. I'm sure it'd do just fine being part of the Legend. And I know lots of groups clamor for it. The lack of an ability (outside of the end-game) to transform into your Horror or a Horror-like form is one of the things I often see people lament. Having the option would be nice; it's not like you have to use it for your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:06:36-07:00","id":856344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=856341#post856341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I accept most of your points as preferences, but this one I think is untrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I disagree. Which is fine.<br /> <br /> I like that Beasts don't transform. I like that there's no apotheosis where the Beast's mastery of the art of fear becomes as crude as 'shapeshift into a giant monster'. Beasts master fear and become one with their horror by understanding that the most terrifying thing in the human psychology is that which you invent yourself. To paraphrase Alfred Hitchcock, you can build suspense and tension by implying and not showing. You stretch it out as the audience fills in the gaps through their own worst, darkest, secret thoughts. Once you show the surprise, it's done. People quickly move on.<br /> <br /> Beasts have maintained the fear by not being the visible surprise. They're tension and suspense and fear.<br /> <br /> Now putting 'shapeshifting monster' into the PG is a mistake, IMO. Many groups may want it, people may lament it. Adding it codifies it into Beast, takes the lesser 'jump scare' path, and diminishes what I think makes the game a masterpiece.<br /> <br /> YMMV. Yours obviously does. Repeating above, this is fine. This is a thread for suggestions and requests. You've done the later, I've made the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:29:12-07:00","id":856351,"title":"","content":"The original <i>Gojira </i>was very much a horror movie, much as many folks think of the campy '60s-'70s Godzilla movies. It drew out the horror and tension by building up both a sense of mystery and the awesome power of the thing to come. Then it finally revealed that power, and even as it lay waste to the city it was no less horrifying. It was one example of the implication leading into the revelation, where both worked and the themes of horror and danger still worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:51:23-07:00","id":856594,"title":"","content":"One idea I had for an alternative power outside of Nightmares and Atavisms is the ability to breed purely animalistic physical incarnations of your Horror, drawing on the nature of the Dark Mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:59:58-07:00","id":856602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=856594#post856594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I had for an alternative power outside of Nightmares and Atavisms is the ability to breed purely animalistic physical incarnations of your Horror, drawing on the nature of the Dark Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps not fully physical but maybe something more like ephemeral beings. Like Unfettered, but able to enter the physical world through Primordial Pathways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:24:37-07:00","id":856612,"title":"","content":"This may trend a bit more into the territory of an ST guide and I think is a must for the book on Lairs, but The Pack is doing it and that seems to be a pretty player oriented book, so I'll suggest it. Could we get a couple more location write ups that highlight the themes and new mechanics of the Player's Guide? The corebook had some pretty awesome stuff and I think we all would love to see more of the world through a Beast's eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:54:31-07:00","id":857343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=856602#post856602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps not fully physical but maybe something more like ephemeral beings. Like Unfettered, but able to enter the physical world through Primordial Pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like your Horror possesses the poor slob whose Chamber he/she/whathaveyou invaded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:06:51-07:00","id":857350,"title":"","content":"One request:<br /> <br /> Can we <i>please </i>have a Merit that represents a Hero your character actually gets along with? Not one of the slayer Heroes, perhaps, but certainly one that shrugs and accepts that maybe you aren't to be judged on what you are but what you do?<br /> <br /> I'm tired of explaining how Heroes not being broken people that seize the idea of Beasts being responsible for everything wrong with their lives is more morally ambiguous than the alternative. <br /> <br /> (my constant refrain is that broken Heroes actually have two morally clean options that present themselves right then and there: Put the rabid dog down before they hurt anyone else, and Get the Hero some help, probably by getting them arrested).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:10:49-07:00","id":857354,"title":"","content":"Is the idea of getting a section dedicated to explaining how to create your own Families or Hungers still on the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:27:22-07:00","id":857819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=855971#post855971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I can think of right off-hand that my group really wants to see is an ability to assume monstrous form. Bonus points if it's customizable like a demon or similar. That gives us a big set of options for &quot;monstrous shapeshifter&quot; types, which would be great for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they do already have one.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't kick in until Lair 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:38:43-07:00","id":857828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=857350#post857350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One request:<br /> <br /> Can we <i>please </i>have a Merit that represents a Hero your character actually gets along with? Not one of the slayer Heroes, perhaps, but certainly one that shrugs and accepts that maybe you aren't to be judged on what you are but what you do?<br /> <br /> I'm tired of explaining how Heroes not being broken people that seize the idea of Beasts being responsible for everything wrong with their lives is more morally ambiguous than the alternative.<br /> <br /> (my constant refrain is that broken Heroes actually have two morally clean options that present themselves right then and there: Put the rabid dog down before they hurt anyone else, and Get the Hero some help, probably by getting them arrested).</div> </div> </div> </div>True Friend+Storyteller permission?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:18:05-07:00","id":858439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=857828#post857828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Friend+Storyteller permission?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's how I'd work it, yeah.<br /> <br /> Folks, this is great. I have a nice long list of stuff to include in the PG, some of which confirmed things I was already considering, some of which were awesome new ideas. Some of it is a better fit for the STG, but hey, it's good to have a head start on that, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:30:46-07:00","id":858485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=858439#post858439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's how I'd work it, yeah.<br /> <br /> Folks, this is great. I have a nice long list of stuff to include in the PG, some of which confirmed things I was already considering, some of which were awesome new ideas. Some of it is a better fit for the STG, but hey, it's good to have a head start on that, too!</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the chances of a very brief outline of the stuff you're thinking of putting in the PG at this point? &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\"