54-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863265#post863265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the ability to burn Satiety to generate the &quot;fuel stat&quot; for your allies if they are running low?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a more costly iteration of Mother's Kiss, possibly, but Family Dinner makes the most basic iteration of this ruinous to the fuel economy of a lot of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:36:52-07:00","id":863356,"title":"","content":"Any way to do something along the lines of &quot;fear of death&quot;. I really enjoy games I can work a good ghost story into. Can fear of death be merged with the fear of self someone else suggested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:07:58-07:00","id":863694,"title":"","content":"I'd especially like:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Expanded rules and discussion on Lairs, traveling the Primordial Pathways, Chamber/Burrow creation and management, imposing Traits on the physical world, the advantages Beasts can gain from environmental immunity, and their significance on a Beast's lifestyle. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">More Atavisms, Advanced/Epic Merits, and Nightmares, in this rough order of priority. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">More discussion on the Inheritances, their use in play, and especially how to use Incarnate Beasts as playable characters (or mentors for lesser Beasts) for those gamers that want them as a high-powered PC or recurring NPC option instead of an endgame condition (and suicide allegory), including expanded guidelines on how to manage one\u2019s Myth. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">More exploration of the Primordial Dream as an environment and ecosystem, and its cosmological relationship with the rest of the Astral and other realms such as the Shadow, the Hedge, or the Underworld and their denizens. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Some exploration of mystical communion/connection with the Dark Mother as an alternative path to power outside of Atavisms, Nightmares, and Lair traits. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">More examples of, and options for, feeding. E.g. feeding on awe, hatred, or lust as well as fear, and options to feed on symbolism and/or narrative significance as well as 'dark' emotions. Options for less directly predatory feeding interactions with mortals, such as being the awesome/fearsome guardian/protector/symbol of a territory or community.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:05:52-07:00","id":863852,"title":"","content":"I have no idea how far this would go for other writers, but while I would like to talk more about the Inheritances as playable options, particularly the Incarnates, I would never, <i>ever </i>remove the suicide allegory. It's a very important element to the Inheritances-to remove the allegory is to ruin the power and pathos of Inheritances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:30:14-07:00","id":863868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863852#post863852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how far this would go for other writers, but while I would like to talk more about the Inheritances as playable options, particularly the Incarnates, I would never, <i>ever </i>remove the suicide allegory. It's a very important element to the Inheritances-to remove the allegory is to ruin the power and pathos of Inheritances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not going to open up a discussion on suicide and so on but i think that some more info on inheritances would be very nice, especially the Incarnate Inheritance as it is the only remotely playable one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:16:18-07:00","id":863929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863852#post863852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how far this would go for other writers, but while I would like to talk more about the Inheritances as playable options, particularly the Incarnates, I would never, <i>ever </i>remove the suicide allegory. It's a very important element to the Inheritances-to remove the allegory is to ruin the power and pathos of Inheritances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, while the other two Inheritances are clearly unplayable and suicide allegories due to their loss of sapience, I struggle a lot to perceive such an allegory in the Incarnate Inheritance. If anything, I tend to perceive the Incarnates as a trascendental state, an allegory for self-empowering life-stage transitions (such as going from childhood to adolescence, or from adolescence to adulthood), and a condition just as playable and relevant to the game setting as vampire elders and archmages. Judging from my personal lens of an amoral, individualistic transhumanist, I see very little of value in conventional morality or mundane mortality (which the Beasts have a rather loose connection with since the Devouring), so I am unable to see what exactly the Incarnates stand to lose in the bargain that is so important as to justify the prevailing interpretation of a suicide allegory. It is not like Incarnates aren't free to mingle with mortals or more likely other supernaturals on non-antagonistic terms whenever they feel the need for companionship, after all, or to keep relevant social ties with individuals from either group (most likely other supernaturals since they understand much more). The transformation essentially seems to remove many of the inherent limitations of the Beast condition, most importantly their constraining connection to the Monomyth on someone else's terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:31:10-07:00","id":863938,"title":"","content":"Your struggle, as well as others, is one of those reasons why I want to dig more into it. Because in some ways, it is a transcendental state. That doesn't stop it being utterly horrific, not the least of which ways is how Beasts effectively just become Heroes.<br /> <br /> Also, archmages are transcendental. Those fuckers should (and do) scare the shit out of anyone under them, and if they could regain clarity long enough to realize what they are, they'd be horrified at themselves.<br /> <br /> Of course, the easiest metaphor is that it's a far more complicated version( in terms of emotional roller coasters and familial questions) of Becoming Nightmare. Transcendental Incarnation may be, but it really is the equivalent of becoming a True Fae. As is, I can see how people would argue for it. I want to make sure people don't lose out.<br /> <br /> As for conventional morality....Ugh, no, I'm done with this particular conversation actually. I don't want it. I'd rather do the supernatural faction for good argument again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:51:21-07:00","id":863945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863929#post863929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to perceive the Incarnates as a trascendental state, an allegory for self-empowering life-stage transitions (such as going from childhood to adolescence, or from adolescence to adulthood)</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the direction a bit backwards there, if the womb allegory didn't tip you off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:01:33-07:00","id":863952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863938#post863938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your struggle, as well as others, is one of those reasons why I want to dig more into it. Because in some ways, it is a transcendental state. That doesn't stop it being utterly horrific, not the least of which ways is how Beasts effectively just become Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The analogy between Incarnates and Heroes seems rather strained to me, since Heroes are in some ways even more slaves to the (corrupted) Monomyth than ordinary Beasts are, while Incarnates are free to define their own relationship with it on their own terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, archmages are transcendental. Those fuckers should (and do) scare the shit out of anyone under them, and if they could regain clarity long enough to realize what they are, they'd be horrified at themselves. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I have even more extreme difficulty from my own perspective to grasp why Archmages (or non-Tremere Liches for that matter) should ever be horrified at themselves, from their own trascendental perspective, than I have with Incarnates, since Archmages don't even have any need for a predatory lifestyle to feed. And such a lifestyle may only feel as a negative from the narrow perspective of a mundane mortal, which need not apply to other sapient entities. I'm sure non-vegan humans would really look horrific to many sapient animals, from their own perspective. Moreover, I find rather questionable to blame Archmages for their lack of clarity, when under pretty much all important accounts they have the most complete and all-encompassing perspective of the universe among the Tellurian denizens ths side of the Abyss. To say they lack clarity in comparison to mortals feels as right to me as to say healthy humans lack clarity in comparison to the deaf, blind, and intellectually-impaired.<br /> <br /> In the end, I'm just making an argument why gaming material to have Incarnates as high-powered PC options, or recurring NPC mentors and such, should exist for those of us who can appreciate their value, just like Imperial Mysteries exists to provide that option for archmages, or Equinox Road for high-powered changelings, or A Thousand Years of Nights is going to do for vampire elders. As things currently stand in the foreseeable development of the gameline, the Player's Guide seems a better place for such rules than most. Of course, should OPP ever decide to do an equivalent of Imperial Mysteries or A Thousand Years of Nights or Equinox Road for BtP focused on Incarnates, my money is already ready to buy it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:05:56-07:00","id":863953,"title":"","content":"So that's the challenge then: Make it so everyone, yourself included, can find the Incarnates horrific, both inside and out.<br /> <br /> It's a daunting task, but I'm willing to try.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, don't get me wrong, no one wants to play an Incarnate more than I do. But it's clear the &quot;I want to play as one&quot; factor is there.<br /> <br /> But the &quot;Incarnates should terrify you&quot; aspect, that seems to be lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-11-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:20:31-07:00","id":863958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863945#post863945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got the direction a bit backwards there, if the womb allegory didn't tip you off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have just as big difficulties to see the Incarnate Inheritance as an allegory for age regression, since I perceive the process as one of self-empowerment, maturation, and liberation under pretty much any relevant aspect. So the only metaphor that seems to apply to the condition in terms of life stages is one of growth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:25:31-07:00","id":863959,"title":"","content":"I suppose the only question I want to ask, for now, is whether you regard the Becoming Nightmare mechanic from the Changeling supplements a positive change or a negative change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:46:40-07:00","id":863964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863959#post863959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the only question I want to ask, for now, is whether you regard the Becoming Nightmare mechanic from the Changeling supplements a positive change or a negative change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so good as Ascension in certain regards, but definitely good. The constraints True Fae are burdened with seem a little price to become an immortal, godlike, transcendental entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:52:27-07:00","id":863967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863964#post863964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so good as Ascension in certain regards, but definitely good. The constraints True Fae are unquestionably burdened with seem a little price to become an immortal, godlike, transcendental entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I think you know I'm the Changeling guy. In case you didn't know, I am the Changeling guy.<br /> <br /> I hope you can appreciate how I Can't Even right now. I hope that makes sense to you. Because I Can't Even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:59:19-07:00","id":863969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863958#post863958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have just as big difficulties to see the Incarnate Inheritance as an allegory for age regression,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not age regression, no, but you'll notice that the monsters in this gameline subtitled &quot;the Primordial&quot; have powers with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atavism\" target=\"_blank\">a particular name</a> that work better in the portion of the cosmology that's explicitly compared to a womb and that the Inheritances in general and the Incarnate Inheritance in particular are described as paths to the Dark Mother, i.e. the being common Begotten thought considers the root of the grand supernatural family tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> since I perceive the process as one of self-empowerment, maturation, and liberation under pretty much any relevant aspect. </div> </div> </div>Terrifying the masses, committing ruthless murder, or laying low your fellow monsters don't strike me as any more &quot;self-empowerment&quot; than Heroes tearing greater hunting shortcuts from their kills, and burying yourself deeper in the well of nightmares and having to maintain a certain image of yourself on pain of universal vulnerability to imposed weakness isn't what I'd call &quot;liberation.&quot;<br /> <br /> And if you want to mature into a more conversational Lernean Hydra, then sure, we can call that &quot;maturation,&quot; but we don't call physically finishing puberty &quot;adulthood&quot; in any laudable sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-11-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:36:08-07:00","id":863986,"title":"","content":"I... I'm still processing the idea that it might be construed <i>as a good thing </i>to become a True Fae. I mean, I'm not the Changeling guy like Arc is, but I'm pretty sure becoming a living narrative, totally constrained by the need for conflict, devoid of true empathy (the Skill of the same name doesn't count. Psychopaths are good at recognizing and manipulating emotions too), for whom the closest thing to a best friend is a sworn enemy because it allows them both to perpetuate their existence, is a Very Bad Thing<sup>TM</sup>. This is still ignoring the fact that the best shortcut to conflict in the life of one of the Gentry is kidnapping people, warping them body, mind, and soul, and then using them as playthings for your own amusement.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the raw terror of the Incarnate needs to be emphasized a bit more. Just mechanically they're unholy terrors, capable of using Gauru-style regeneration, adding their Lair to Strength, or gaining their Lair in Armour. This is still not counting any benefits that come from wielding Atavisms that start to get really rather silly at those levels, like Limb from Limb, Dragonfire, Storm-Lashed, Cyclopean Strength, and Titanic Blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:54:54-07:00","id":863998,"title":"","content":"Anyway, onto less heated argument causing matters, it might be interesting to have a section that explores in depth on what sort of benefits a Begotten can provide to their various PC splat kin and what sort of benefits allying with those creatures has for the Beast. Not sure if it's workable, but it's an interesting thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:58:56-07:00","id":863999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863969#post863969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not age regression, no, but you'll notice that the monsters in this gameline subtitled &quot;the Primordial&quot; have powers with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atavism\" target=\"_blank\">a particular name</a> that work better in the portion of the cosmology that's explicitly compared to a womb and that the Inheritances in general and the Incarnate Inheritance in particular are described as paths to the Dark Mother, i.e. the being common Begotten thought considers the root of the grand supernatural family tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Begotten really seem to have taken their Kinship powers as far too much an excuse to develop a terribly exaggerated notion of their importance in the supernatural ecology of the Tellurian. Whatever the Dark Mother really is, be it the Primordial Dream itself (or its self-aware component, if any), the first and best of the Incarnates, or whatever developmental stage exists for the Begotten beyond Incarnation (say it might be for the Begotten what Ascension is for mages, if Incarnate is the Archmage equivalent), almost certainly it isn't the root cause of all the supernaturals. As it concerns the name for Atavisms, it would be fairly easy to call them &quot;Enhancements&quot; or somesuch, if you reimagine the Begotten as some kind of mystically-empowered superhumans. After all, in the end they are just another kind of supernatural-human hybrid existing in a symbiontic relationship like the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Terrifying the masses, committing ruthless murder, or laying low your fellow monsters don't strike me as any more &quot;self-empowerment&quot; than Heroes tearing greater hunting shortcuts from their kills, and burying yourself deeper in the well of nightmares and having to maintain a certain image of yourself on pain of universal vulnerability to imposed weakness isn't what I'd call &quot;liberation.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Really, if you want to make an argument about this kind of issue that makes any sense from my perspective you should avoid any appeal to the inherent value of conventional morality or mundane mortality. Anyway, I may point out that Incarnates seem much more free to define their lifestyle according to their own terms than Heroes or ordinary Beasts, including potentially satisfying their Satiety feeding needs in terms that aren't especially predatory if they so choose, since they don't have to fear the Ravenous or Slumbering conditions. To have to maintain a certain image of yourself seems little price for immortality, vast supernatural power, and liberation from most constraints Heroes and ordinary Beasts work under. Otherwise, sure, Incarnates have to maintain a predatory lifestyle to some degree. So what ? I'm sure humans would look like horrific monsters to sapient farm animals, and I'm not going to embrace the vegan lifestyle in the foreseeable future because of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:06:59-07:00","id":864004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863964#post863964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so good as Ascension in certain regards, but definitely good. The constraints True Fae are burdened with seem a little price to become an immortal, godlike, transcendental entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am <i>not</i> the <b>Changeling</b> guy, and <i>what</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:31:16-07:00","id":864022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863999#post863999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Begotten really seem to have taken their Kinship powers as far too much an excuse to develop a terribly exaggerated notion of their importance in the supernatural ecology of the Tellurian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your decision to attribute importance to age is irrelevant. They're metaphysically basic and cosmologically far-reaching and the simplest explanation that presents itself is that this is because they're offshoots of the ever-changing proto-monster from the dawn of time and/or the birth of human consciousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever the Dark Mother really is, be it the Primordial Dream itself (or its self-aware component, if any), the first and best of the Incarnates, or whatever developmental stage exists for the Begotten beyond Incarnation (say it might be for the Begotten what Ascension is for mages, if Incarnate is the Archmage equivalent), almost certainly it isn't the root cause of all the supernaturals. </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. She touches almost every corner of the metaphysics and her attributed proximity to the source of human fear is on account of her Children's inherited lack of developed and refined supernatural abilities. Other monsters get to be more complex as they work their way closer to their respective supernatural zeniths. Not so the Begotten, who simply amass a larger collection of building blocks with which to operate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it concerns the name for Atavisms, it would be fairly easy to call them &quot;Enhancements&quot; or somesuch, if you reimagine the Begotten as some kind of mystically-empowered superhumans. After all, in the end they are just another kind of supernatural-human hybrid existing in a symbiontic relationship like the Sin-Eaters. </div> </div> </div>I really couldn't care less about how you'd &quot;reimagine&quot; anything in this thread that concerns material for the Player's Guide for the game as it's actually written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, if you want to make an argument about this kind of issue that makes any sense from my perspective you should avoid any appeal to the inherent value of conventional morality or mundane mortality. </div> </div> </div>There is zero appeal to morality of any sort in highlighting the lack of freedom and self-sufficiency in needing to maintain connections to others under the constraints of a very definite role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:39:31-07:00","id":864024,"title":"","content":"What's it like to have an ancient horror devour devour you and be your horror? e.g. Medusa","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:09:27-07:00","id":864038,"title":"","content":"I'll be blunt and straightforward, Iri: the mentality you you approach this game with is not shared by Matt. Dude's a moral humanist, I've seen that time and again, and that's literally just the beginning of the differences in mentalities, in terms of game design and cosmological functions. Several of the writers also take this tact. And that's before you even account that the Chronicles of Darkness on the whole takes an stance in opposition to you as a horror game with moral and humanist questions at its' foundation.<br /> <br /> If you have fun with the game regardless, great! But we're probably not going to play wish-fulfillment for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:14:33-07:00","id":864041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=863986#post863986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure becoming a living narrative, totally constrained by the need for conflict,</div> </div> </div> </div>And these are the kind of constraints I acknowledge as a significant burden and make me regard True Faehood as a transcendental state less desirable than Ascension or even the Incarnate Inheritance. Nonetheless, still an acceptable price for godlike immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> devoid of true empathy (the Skill of the same name doesn't count. Psychopaths are good at recognizing and manipulating emotions too), </div> </div> </div>Little self-disclosure: I'm a high-functioning person with robust sociopathic traits except lack of self-control, a need for extraordinary stimulation, or an especially shallow conditional affect. All my entire life experience has utterly failed to persuade me that this empathy you talk of is but a serious burden to one's serenity, happiness, self-direction, rationality, and efficiency. I seem to enjoy all those things more than most other people I know, and I'm challenged to think of anything really more malicious in my lifestyle than ignoring beggars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> for whom the closest thing to a best friend is a sworn enemy because it allows them both to perpetuate their existence </div> </div> </div>Well, if Existence is Struggle as our AA friends would say, it makes some sense to assume a friendly enemy is one of the most reilable relationships there is. I can think of various fictional examples of characters and societies that embrace the idea the best friend is a friendly rival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is still ignoring the fact that the best shortcut to conflict in the life of one of the Gentry is kidnapping people, warping them body, mind, and soul, and then using them as playthings for your own amusement. </div> </div> </div>Putting aside the whole lack of consent issue, try looking at the whole issue from the perspective that being a changeling or a True Fae is better than being a mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, the raw terror of the Incarnate needs to be emphasized a bit more. Just mechanically they're unholy terrors, capable of using Gauru-style regeneration, adding their Lair to Strength, or gaining their Lair in Armour. This is still not counting any benefits that come from wielding Atavisms that start to get really rather silly at those levels, like Limb from Limb, Dragonfire, Storm-Lashed, Cyclopean Strength, and Titanic Blow. </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the immunity to Anathemas and to the Ravenous and Slumbering Conditions, the ability to travel the Primordial Dream at will, and true immortality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:29:10-07:00","id":864046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864038#post864038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be blunt and straightforward, Iri: the mentality you you approach this game with is not shared by Matt. Dude's a moral humanist, I've seen that time and again, and that's literally just the beginning of the differences in mentalities, in terms of game design and cosmological functions. Several of the writers also take this tact. And that's before you even account that the Chronicles of Darkness on the whole takes an stance in opposition to you as a horror game with moral and humanist questions at its' foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know, I know. I have been having this kind of argument about WoD games pretty much since they existed, and I've gotten accustomed to the need to filter them according to my own personal lens in order to get any amusement or usefulness from them, typically rewriting them as a mix of fantasy, action-adventure, intrigue, and mystery. Apart from anything else, my personality makes me unable to get horror as a genre. I just like to play Devil's Advocate to remind you people the kind of me exists in the gamer base. I just get alternatively amused, annoyed, and puzzled a lot when WoD published material has tried hard in the past to pretend people with a RL personality and values like mine don't exist in this fictional universe because themes. This may get personal because it's kind of telling me I couldn't or shouldn't exist at a certain level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:31:09-07:00","id":864047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864041#post864041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little self-disclosure: I'm a high-functioning person with robust sociopathic traits except lack of self-control, a need for extraordinary stimulation, or an especially shallow conditional affect. All my entire life experience has utterly failed to persuade me that this empathy you talk of is but a serious burden to one's serenity, happiness, self-direction, rationality, and efficiency. I seem to enjoy all those things more than most other people I know, and I'm challenged to think of anything really more malicious in my lifestyle than ignoring beggars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so, I have/had no intention of offending you, and I have no intention of pursuing this debate since I have little to no technical knowledge as to the intricacies of how sociopathic tendencies and psychopathy actually relate. However, I would posit that the traits you point out that you <i>don't </i>possess <i>are </i>those possessed by the True Fae. In fact, they're the traits that more or less <i>define </i>the True Fae. Also, the narrative constraints are being a little undersold here, I think. An Actor is stuck as that single story, and no matter how it is reshaped, it remains a single story. Self-direction, rationality, and efficiency go out the window when you need to abide by Frailties and are incapable of changing anything but the presentation of your core identity.<br /> <br /> That being said, from an objective stance, I can see how being a Changeling is desirable, and how it can be seen as a superior state to baseline humanity. The idea of a non-malicious Durance was discussed in the Changeling forums a while back, along with the social implications being one such lucky member of the Lost would have amongst others with a totally non-consensual stay in Faerie. That being said, I disagree that the True Fae are superior simply for raw power and immortality- barring things like Titles, I think it would be better to be a Wyrd 10 Changeling than a True Fae- at least you'd still have your free will. That being said, I'll leave the Changeling talk to the more well-informed, like Arc and Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:39:08-07:00","id":864053,"title":"","content":"Iri, so long as you understand where you're at in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> I think it's apparent I disagree with Iri, but I want it clear I have written ten-to-twenty page essays for college on all the reasons why no one would want to be True Fae.<br /> <br /> Granted, it wasn't done in the context <i>of</i> the True Fae. It was dealing with everything Becoming Nightmare represents, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:06:18-07:00","id":864066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864047#post864047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, so, I have/had no intention of offending you,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry. You haven't gotten any close to offending me. As I said, the only real way WoD writers got to that in the past is when they apparently tried hard to pretend the equivalent of well-adjusted low-empathy people like me couldn't or shouldn't exist in their fictional universe because themes, since it implied a denial of my RL existence or life experience in a certain sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I would posit that the traits you point out that you <i>don't </i>possess <i>are </i>those possessed by the True Fae. In fact, they're the traits that more or less <i>define </i>the True Fae. Also, the narrative constraints are being a little undersold here, I think. An Actor is stuck as that single story, and no matter how it is reshaped, it remains a single story. Self-direction, rationality, and efficiency go out the window when you need to abide by Frailties and are incapable of changing anything but the presentation of your core identity. </div> </div> </div>True, these factors are among the factual constraints and drawbacks I acknowledge about the True Fae condition. As a matter of fact, coming back closer to our original topic, I see reason to argue the Incarnate Inheritance is a more desirable way of supernatural trascendence than True Faehood, because the former seems more self-directed than the latter, even if the former seems theoretically less vulnerable to destruction. Roughly speaking, I'd rate several 'advanced' WoD supernatural conditions with immortality and substantial supernatural power this way, in order of preferability: Ascension/Archmage &gt; Incarnate Inheritance &gt; Purified/Reborn/Eternal with psychic powers &gt; True Fae &gt; vampire elder &gt; other kinds of Immortals. I know too little about Mummies and Demons to make a reasoned comparison, and I'm not sure if Sin-Eaters ever get a way of their own to get any kind of equivalent condition. So far, I'm honestly challenged to think of any real drawbacks to the uber-mage or uber-beast conditions that aren't based in an appeal to the inherent value of morality, humanism, or empathy with baseline humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, I disagree that the True Fae are superior simply for raw power and immortality- barring things like Titles, I think it would be better to be a Wyrd 10 Changeling than a True Fae- at least you'd still have your free will. </div> </div> </div>A fair point, but then again, my whole argument about this was that True Fae may be seen as preferable to baseline humanity if that gets to be the choice. As far as I can tell, the Gentry are not entirely devoid of free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-11-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:48:07-07:00","id":864080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864041#post864041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the immunity to Anathemas and to the Ravenous and Slumbering Conditions, the ability to travel the Primordial Dream at will, and <b>true immortality.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That Jim Fisher mentioned he'd consider this when you last mentioned it to him has not translated into it becoming a facet of the Inheritance in the final print.<br /> <br /> Back on topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternate Birthrights have already been brought up, but more stuff to do with Mother's Kiss and/or Family Ties would also be neat, I think. Maybe something like giving characters particular Merits?<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, more Advanced and Epic Merits are always welcome. Possibly Hunger-specific Merits, as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-11-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:30:46-07:00","id":864108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864080#post864080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Jim Fisher mentioned he'd consider this when you last mentioned it to him has not translated into it becoming a facet of the Inheritance in the final print.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not explictly denied, either. The writeup remains silent on the issue, and it's implied true immortality (which may well mean something more than agelessness) is at least something Incarnates may work towards, and they are not subject to the limits of lesser Beasts and/or may develop more advanced powers beyond what is described in the template (e.g. this may be a good idea for an Incarnate-only Atavism or Merit). But I agree this kind of detail may indeed require something more than the corebook writeup. Another example is some guidelines on how to stabilize your Myth when it gets threatened.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:12:12-07:00","id":864138,"title":"","content":"Another idea might be to have some kind of optional equivalent to vampire bloodlines, mage legacies, and changeling entitlements, perhaps based on preferred Lessons. Yes, I know lessons Beasts embrace originally arose as psychological constructs to give significance to their existence beyond the demands of Hunger. This doesn't necessarily mean they are unable to force the universe to give mystical significance to their choices with sufficient dedication, kinda like it happened with many vampire covenants and mage orders. Or perhaps the same could instead be done for Hungers, following the latter analogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-12-2016, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:06:44-07:00","id":864246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864041#post864041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little self-disclosure: I'm a high-functioning person with robust sociopathic traits except lack of self-control, a need for extraordinary stimulation, or an especially shallow conditional affect. All my entire life experience has utterly failed to persuade me that this empathy you talk of is but a serious burden to one's serenity, happiness, self-direction, rationality, and efficiency. I seem to enjoy all those things more than most other people I know, and I'm challenged to think of anything really more malicious in my lifestyle than ignoring beggars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience helping others can provide a deep, existential pleasure that is hard to top. I think the pain it can bring is more than worth the price. There is a reason the phrase &quot;to give is better than to receive&quot; came about after all. Than again, that might just be me.<br /> <br /> As for the Inheritances, a section going into greater depth on them would be cool, but it sounds like something that would work better in the Storytellers section. While playing a game about being an Incarnate could be a lot of fun if done right, but they are more meant to be used as NPCs and if played would work better as a solo game.<br /> <br /> As far as being one is concerned, depending on your temperament and outlook, I could definitely see the appeal. The benefits are rather tempting, although I don't think it is worth the change in personality or restrictions on the ability to change it would bring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","user":"Xenorath","date":". 04-12-2016, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:03:45-07:00","id":864470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864246#post864246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience helping others can provide a deep, existential pleasure that is hard to top. I think the pain it can bring is more than worth the price. There is a reason the phrase &quot;to give is better than to receive&quot; came about after all. Than again, that might just be me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps for others but not really so from my own perspective. While I find it is certainly pleasant to make people little acts of kindness that do not greatly burden oneself out of getting their respect and gratitude, I also find myself being good providing a lot of sincere affection (even if entirely conditional in the end) to select people I've grown to regard worthy of my love and care, to cope quickly and efficiently with loss and separation, to be almost immune to fear (reason I'm unable to appreciate horror), anxiety, guilt, and remorse (except for failure at my own self-imposed standards), to be just as happy at a party or alone. On the other hand, I care little for the supposed inherent value of the life, happiness, and feelings of random strangers that threaten my own, I find nothing wrong with using people as objects in appropriate circumstances, and I'm sure I'd able to do acts of extreme ruthlessness with a smile if necessary to protect my interests or my ideals. Yet out of enlightened self-interest, rational selfishness, and care for certain abstract ideals I'm rather fond of, I'm often supportive of policies and lifestyles that pursue the greater good as I understand it and make society at large as happy, free, prosperous, efficient, rational, and advanced as possible. Honestly from life experience I deem this kind of personality may give one more potential self-direction, serenity, and freedom of action in life, to be just as good and happy being a physician or a soldier as circumstances dictate, so I'm greatly challenged to see the alternative as a gain instead of a loss. If anything, I get rather annoyed when society attempts to impose me to feel or fake a sensibility I'm unable, unwilling, or uncaring to show (this is the reason I greatly hate and resent PC and SJWs and I'm rather fond and jealous of my universe-given right to be an equal-opportunity callous, unsensitive, selfish, outspoken misanthrophe) or when it assumes I'm unable to have an happy, productive, well-adjusted lifestyle because of my personality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Inheritances, a section going into greater depth on them would be cool, but it sounds like something that would work better in the Storytellers section. While playing a game about being an Incarnate could be a lot of fun if done right, but they are more meant to be used as NPCs and if played would work better as a solo game. </div> </div> </div>Well, I support greater use of Incarnate Beasts both as high-powered PC options for those players that are willing and able to use and appreciate them, and as recurrent NPC mentors, bodhisattvas , and talking, walking polot hooks in other cases. I deem to limit them to be boss antagonists is a serious waste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as being one is concerned, depending on your temperament and outlook, I could definitely see the appeal. The benefits are rather tempting, although I don't think it is worth the change in personality or restrictions on the ability to change it would bring. </div> </div> </div>This is another point that leaves me rather perplexed. Choice of one's Myth seems largely determined by the Beast's actions and I would assume an Incarnate would even be able to make some further adjustments to it over time if wanted to. To lose one's Legend and Life means those things are not so central anymore to one's being to be source of Willpower, but it's not like the character suddenly becomes unable to care about the things they represent, especially if they aren't in conflict with the Myth. E.g. if one's Myth is to be the Hunter of the Guilty, it's not like this going to make a character unable of loyalty or sincerity, even if they stop being a WP refill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-12-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:35:38-07:00","id":864496,"title":"","content":"I hate to do this since I'm the one who instigated this, but if we're going to have this conversation, can we have it in another thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:48:05-07:00","id":864499,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Back on topic.</i></b><br /> <br /> Not sure if this'd be more the domain of the STG, but ways the Begotten might adapt to the more mutable realms of the cosmology could bear further examination. Similarly, what effects do Family Ties have on the Astral mobility of monsters that are otherwise barred from the Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:36:50-07:00","id":864538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864499#post864499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this'd be more the domain of the STG, but ways the Begotten might adapt to the more mutable realms of the cosmology could bear further examination. Similarly, what effects do Family Ties have on the Astral mobility of monsters that are otherwise barred from the Temenos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. I think greater examination of the relationship (and travel endeavours) of the Begotten in realms like the Shadow, Hedge, Underworld, and the Anima Mundi is totally warranted. It seems to me Beasts should fit in the Anima Mundi, to quote but one example, just as easily in a mystical sense as they do in the Temenos, if all this 'primal' stuff is anything but idle talk, yet how would they cope with the Ecstatic Wind ? On the other hand, what effects do Family Ties have on the mobility of Beasts in realms they do not normally travel easily ?<br /> <br /> These kind of concerns make me think perhaps some kind of 'Beast magic' may be warranted to deal with mystical effects that do not really fit among Atavisms, Nightmares, Merits, and Lair Traits. If certain vampires have been able to develop a whole magical school out of their supposed mystical dedication with their own version of a 'Dark Mother', why not the Begotten ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:46:26-07:00","id":864547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864538#post864538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These kind of concerns make me think perhaps some kind of 'Beast magic' may be warranted to deal with mystical effects that do not really fit among Atavisms, Nightmares, Merits, and Lair Traits. If certain vampires have been able to develop a whole magical school out of their supposed mystical dedication with their own version of a 'Dark Mother', why not the Begotten ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this as a kind of conceptual extension and combination of imposing lair Traits and Nightmares. Instead of bringing a part of your Lair into the world, you pull a concept of the thing you want to accomplish out of the Dream and, by spending Satiety, clothe it in physical (or ephemeral, or Wyrd) reality. I'm not sure exactly what you could do with it however and I think that it might fit better in the STG or something similar to Sacraments and Blasphemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:06:03-07:00","id":864556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864547#post864547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see this as a kind of conceptual extension and combination of imposing lair Traits and Nightmares. Instead of bringing a part of your Lair into the world, you pull a concept of the thing you want to accomplish out of the Dream and, by spending Satiety, clothe it in physical (or ephemeral, or Wyrd) reality. I'm not sure exactly what you could do with it however and I think that it might fit better in the STG or something similar to Sacraments and Blasphemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea seems good, and it might well be the base for a whole new supplement like SaB, but it seems like something certain PC would use regularly, so it doesn't fit the STG, just like additional Atavisms, Nightmares, Merits, and Lair Traits don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:38:36-07:00","id":864582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864547#post864547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see this as a kind of conceptual extension and combination of imposing lair Traits and Nightmares. Instead of bringing a part of your Lair into the world, you pull a concept of the thing you want to accomplish out of the Dream and, by spending Satiety, clothe it in physical (or ephemeral, or Wyrd) reality. I'm not sure exactly what you could do with it however and I think that it might fit better in the STG or something similar to Sacraments and Blasphemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I had a similar idea, except I didn't think of it as a power for the Begotten. More specifically, I thought of it as the core ability of a minor template I've so far been calling &quot;Nightmare Shamans&quot; (a working title). The idea is that they're people who through innate ability or through the sort of vision-questing mentioned in the Hunter crossover section, have developed a link to the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Strange minds think alike, I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T07:12:30-07:00","id":864906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864582#post864582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, I had a similar idea, except I didn't think of it as a power for the Begotten. More specifically, I thought of it as the core ability of a minor template I've so far been calling &quot;Nightmare Shamans&quot; (a working title). The idea is that they're people who through innate ability or through the sort of vision-questing mentioned in the Hunter crossover section, have developed a link to the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Strange minds think alike, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I'll have a go at writing this up as a homebrew. I'll write it as a series of Merits, so either a Beast or a 'nightmare shaman' can use it (although Beasts get a slightly different version reliant on Satiety as opposed to a Shaman using Willpower). I'm going to write the 'magic' as being quite 'mythic' as in it's the kind of stuff you get in myths. Probably lots of fairly subtly enchanted items, blessings, curses, possibly some Circe/Medea-esque 'magic potions' enhanced by the power of the Dream. Sound OK? Any input on the soon-to-be-thread would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry for hijacking the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T06:24:43-07:00","id":865916,"title":"","content":"How about a death curse? Like, should the hero slay the Beast while said-curse is active, s/he will in turn become a beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T09:59:12-07:00","id":865990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=865916#post865916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a death curse? Like, should the hero slay the Beast while said-curse is active, s/he will in turn become a beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some other misfortune maybe, but turning into a Beast goes against the vibe that Heros and Beasts were &quot;in waiting&quot; for their conditions before they ostensibly happened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T01:56:26-07:00","id":866317,"title":"","content":"Expanding the game as a Slumbering beast?<br /> Can she &quot;reject&quot; her horror at somepoint?<br /> How about a beast that want to live a satiety 10 because HATE own horror so much?<br /> More option , mabye a specific minor template?, could be interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T06:13:55-07:00","id":866360,"title":"","content":"How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:04:22-07:00","id":866372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=866360#post866360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of those kind of fall under Ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:11:09-07:00","id":866374,"title":"","content":"Some more stuff for messing around in the dreams of other beings might be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:18:56-07:00","id":866377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=866372#post866372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both of those kind of fall under Ruin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ruin suggests entropy and destruction. Chaos isn't necessarily that. It can suggest change, sudden complications, happenstance, etc. Besides, ruin is a Hunger, not a Fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:20:52-07:00","id":866378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=866374#post866374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more stuff for messing around in the dreams of other beings might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, a more solid system for dream-combat and such, ala Changeling, would be very nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:12:33-07:00","id":866520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=866360#post866360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not a bad idea. I could even see combining the two into one. Why not post it up in the Missing Families / Hungers Thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers\"> Missing Families/Hungers - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> OK, one more Player's Guide-related post, but this one is specific so, new thread. Do you think there are any Families and/or Hungers that are unique enough and different enough from the ones in the Beast book to merit writing up? We designed them both to be pretty broad and pretty iconic, but I'm often surprised at the shit I don't think of. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T01:39:27-07:00","id":867437,"title":"","content":"Those nightmare shamans you reference sound like the non-slayer Heroes. Heroes expanding into that territory would be cool, but ultimately an ST guide thing. I like the idea of Beast magic. Maybe its more like changeling 1e's &quot;dusk magic&quot;, where they took existing powers/traits (In this case, lair traits, kinship, oneiromancy) and gave unique and quirky ways of doing it. Like.. new lair traits that attune beasts to the otherworlds, those reverse/blessing family ties. It could be fun to have a new subsystem of powers, but it could just as easily just be a creative use of the existing frameworks. Like, I could see a major lair trait for the hedge--Due to lair trait immunity, the beast isnt as disoriented by the paths, the thorns don't strip whole chunks of satiety away, when used on earth it exposes the meins of fae who are present, and in the Lair it creates a sort of blurred zone between the Hedge and the Temenos that screws with visitor's heads and hearts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T01:23:34-07:00","id":872211,"title":"","content":"Hmm . . . dealing with Horrors that aren't Beasts - that could be worth exploring. There could be some very iconic moments, bargaining with a cadre of nightmarish creatures . . .<br /> <br /> And is it just me, or does anyone else want a &quot;Sea of Nightmares&quot; in the Primordial Dream? Somewhere that a Beast can go, diving deep into the mirrorblack waters of the human subconscious to divine the dark secrets of their foes. To drink deep of its black wisdom, and learn the hidden truths known only to madmen . . .<br /> <br /> Possibly in conjunction with the &quot;Sea of Nightmares&quot;, it seems thematically appropriate for a Beast to be able to wrap themselves in the personal fears of a target. To become - at least for a scene - someone's personal nightmare. Nothing physically changes, but the target experiences the Beast as a living avatar of everything that scares them.<br /> <br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Achaean slowly smiles to himself. Tonight, his enemies will die, executed before his very eyes. His rivals will swear mystically binding oaths, committing themselves to his eternal service. By dawn, he'll be the most powerful mage on the East Coast!<br /> <br /> The assembled mages watch on nervously, as the condemned kneel in a line before the Achaean. Naked, in chains, bearing clear signs of torture, everyone tries desperately to avoid making eye contact with them. The Achaean, feeling magnanimous, offers them a chance to speak in their defense . . . to plead for mercy that will never come.<br /> <br /> One lifts his head, and spits out a mouthful of blood. &quot;We are not defeated. One of us is still free.&quot;<br /> <br /> Laughing, the Achaean steps down, and grabs his hair, yanking the poor unfortunate's head up. &quot;Oh,&quot; the Achaean snears, &quot;and what can one man do?&quot; He punches the man in the face. Teeth go flying.<br /> <br /> &quot;Toby!&quot; The Achaean's head jerks around. No has called him that since he was a boy . . . Not since </div> </div> </div></i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>he</b><i> died . . .<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't hide from me, boy!&quot;<br /> <br /> A smell hits the Achaean's nose, as some sort of commotion breaks out in the audience. The stench of sweat, and cheap whiskey. A smell that had once terrified him. He knew that smell. It was </i><b>his</b><i> smell, after he'd been drinking . . .<br /> <br /> &quot;Get out here, Toby!&quot; The voice roars. A voice he'd hoped never again to hear this side of hell. &quot;Be a man for once in your damn life. Get out here, and take your punishment!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dad?&quot; The Achaean whispers.<br /> <br /> The sound of leather smacking against a well-calloused wrist. </i><b>The belt!</b><i> Some part of the Achaean's mind screamed. </i><b>He's already got the belt out!</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Toby!&quot; A man pushes his way through the crowd. At first, the Achaean can't quite make out his face . . . but then! Its his father! A man dead twenty years. A man he'd personally killed!</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Toby!&quot;<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> Years later, mages still talk about how the smell of urine had filled the room, as the Achaean - most feared mage in the city! - had collapsed to his knees and begged the stranger for mercy. About how the stranger had said not a word, but simply picked up one of the Achaean's prisoners, slung him over his shoulder, and led the rest out of the meeting hall. </i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Anyone know why the system is automatically ending one quote box, and starting another, in mid-sentence? I've been trying, and can't get rid of it - even by putting an alternate set in myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 04-23-2016, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:28:15-07:00","id":873131,"title":"","content":"I can't recall if this's been said, but I'd like more on why you think you've always been the monster when the horror seems to be a separate entity. Linking relevant discussion for point of confusion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/870385-which-cofd-splat-would-you-most-like-or-least-hate-to-be?p=873130#post873130\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...130#post873130</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T11:35:00-07:00","id":873192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=872211#post872211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know why the system is automatically ending one quote box, and starting another, in mid-sentence? I've been trying, and can't get rid of it - even by putting an alternate set in myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be a limit to the number of quote boxes and the size of the quotes that the forum's client software can handle (probably some web/client dev in their infinite wisdom hardcoded some values because they couldn't imagine scenarios that required different values). Has nothing to do with OPP's IT dept. though, just an inherent limitation of this BBS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:22:49-07:00","id":873855,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, are there any special rules for Beasts feeding on other Beasts? Apexes in particular I figure would be prone to it (Tyrants ruling the Hive with an iron fist, Hoarders exerting &quot;taxes&quot;, Nemeses acting as feared arms of inter-Begotten Justice, etc). If that hasn't been discussed it's definitely worth talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:26:06-07:00","id":873857,"title":"","content":"All that comes to mind is: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not every Apex is beneficent. Some of them use the<br /> connection that the hive grants as a way to invade other Beasts\u2019<br /> Lairs, establishing themselves as dominant and forcing them<br /> to provide food for the Apex\u2019s Horror. Some use this kind of<br /> brutality as a step in their quest for the Incarnate Inheritance. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:39:18-07:00","id":873903,"title":"","content":"Ok, so that confirms that Beasts can feed on each other. I think that's worth further discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T18:51:33-07:00","id":874164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=873903#post873903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so that confirms that Beasts can feed on each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It confirms that Beasts can be fed by characters other than themselves, which we knew from the penalty to Satiety potential in the section on feeding rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:54:24-07:00","id":875052,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting to see something like a toned-down version of the Incarnate Inheritance, a capacity to briefly bring the Horror fully into the world...or at least enough into the world that people see The Horror and not Phil From Human Resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:07:35-07:00","id":875071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=875052#post875052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be interesting to see something like a toned-down version of the Incarnate Inheritance, a capacity to briefly bring the Horror fully into the world...or at least enough into the world that people see The Horror and not Phil From Human Resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally half the purpose of opening a Primordial Pathway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:34:03-07:00","id":875141,"title":"","content":"So what's the thinking then on Beasts feeding via other Beasts?<br /> <br /> - it's a normal occurance<br /> - it works normally but is frowned upon/taboo<br /> - it's impossible<br /> - it deserves its own system as something powerful but corruptive or dangerous like diablerie","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:17:33-07:00","id":875185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=875141#post875141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the thinking then on Beasts feeding via other Beasts?<br /> <br /> - it's a normal occurance<br /> - it works normally but is frowned upon/taboo<br /> - it's impossible<br /> - it deserves its own system as something powerful but corruptive or dangerous like diablerie</div> </div> </div> </div>The thinking is Page 243, Sentence 2.<br /> <br /> Removing someone from the pool of direct available Satiety resources makes Devouring a logistical risk even if you circumvent the issue of creating competition and helps underline how the Incarnate are more than just Bigger Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:00:06-07:00","id":875641,"title":"","content":"Some more talk on Lairs might be cool. Is it possible for someone to actually eek out a life in a Lair, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T13:29:08-07:00","id":878046,"title":"","content":"Do we have anything for Beasts with multiple heads, like the hydra, etten, or similar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T14:05:41-07:00","id":878077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=878046#post878046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have anything for Beasts with multiple heads, like the hydra, etten, or similar?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a really cool potential Atavism right there. Probably Namtaru <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:23:18-07:00","id":878387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=878046#post878046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have anything for Beasts with multiple heads, like the hydra, etten, or similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a number of existing Atavisms that cover the practical benefits of such anatomy, as well as a Beast-Shape benefit for the Incarnate.<br /> <br /> What did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:32:40-07:00","id":878438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=878387#post878387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have a number of existing Atavisms that cover the practical benefits of such anatomy, as well as a Beast-Shape benefit for the Incarnate.<br /> <br /> What did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what if a Beast had two minds, which, at a glance seems like classic Dissociative Identity Disorder, but allowed for some kind of benefit, like it's more difficult to influence them supernaturally or for Heroes to get a bead on.<br /> <br /> Another instance might be: what if there are twin beasts, or more bizzarely, a familial brood somehow manages to merge their horror's temporarily to appear as a &quot;multi-headed&quot; monstrosity. Honestly, I don't have anything concrete to offer, was just curious on how people'd implement the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T21:56:22-07:00","id":879907,"title":"","content":"I would like to see alternate ways for people to become Beasts.Play around with the Family idea alittle,like using the Homecoming from the original draft of Beast as an alternate system.Not everyone joins a family the same way after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/f6wpurj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/5hsbn8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/249-nitemare17","name":"Nitemare17","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:10:11-07:00","id":905421,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the minor necro, but is there any material in Beast on noteworthy or mythological Horrors, possibly those that have had multiple hosts? It's one thing to say &quot;a hungry thing of tentacles and eyes&quot; and quite another to say &quot;oh shit, I might have Charbydis in my soul.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:02:38-07:00","id":905570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=905421#post905421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for the minor necro, but is there any material in Beast on noteworthy or mythological Horrors, possibly those that have had multiple hosts? It's one thing to say &amp;quot;a hungry thing of tentacles and eyes&amp;quot; and quite another to say &amp;quot;oh shit, I might have Charbydis in my soul.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Advanced Fame Merit. Unfortunately it's locked behind having actual Fame, so it's not open to as many character concepts. Of course, that's just a way to gain mechanical benefits from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:21:45-07:00","id":905577,"title":"","content":"I think Beasts or Beast like beings for other Primordial Emotions would be cool.<br /> <br /> New crossover nightmares would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:53:39-07:00","id":923959,"title":"","content":"I would like some more support and information for <i>The Horror Itself</i>.<br /> <br /> The basic concept is really cool. Lead them to a place that has some resonance with you lair, open the Primordial Pathway and merge with your horror. Turn around and see them cower in fear. The example on p.98 is one of the things that sold me on Beast.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, after reading the box The Horror Itself I am under the impression that a Beast merged with his horror is much weaker than before, at least at the lower levels of lair.<br /> <br /> If you take the example of the towering giant on p. 98, let's assume he has Strength 4, Dexterity 3 and Stamina 3, Wits 2 and Resolve 3. Size is 5, Lair is 2. He has Brawl 3 and Defensive Combat: Brawl. If not merged with the Horror, that gives him 7 dice for close combat, Defense 5 (Lower of Dex/Wits + Brawl) and 8 health levels (Stamina+Size).<br /> <br /> Now he merges with his Horror, a \u201etowering giant\u201c. His combat dice pool is reduced to 4 (Strength = Power) as Brawl does no longer apply. His defense is only 3 (lower of Power/Finesse) and he has health 5 (Resolve 3 + 2 Lair). Even if you distribute 4 points among Power and Finesse (size does not matter to the Horror game-mechanic-wise), you are weaker than the Beast was in its human form. It gets absurd if you consider the Beast has Looming Presence. In human form the Beast gets an additional 4 health (Lair x2 size) for a total of 12 in the example above. As size does not matter to the Horror game-mechanic-wise, it stays at 5 health. It just looses the size = health advantage of Looming Presence. Add to this the fact that the merged Beast/Horror cannot use Nightmares, and the cool example turns into a nightmare for the Beast if the hunters were actually capable.<br /> <br /> I would really appreciate if the Players Handbook could help somewhat with that dilemma.<br /> <br /> Also, a Horror character sheet page would also be appreciated, as the Horror is quite different from the Beast. Instead of having to make calculations when the action starts, the Horror's stats really should appear on the players character sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 06-30-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:19:27-07:00","id":923978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=923959#post923959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now he merges with his Horror, a \u201etowering giant\u201c. His combat dice pool is reduced to 4 (Strength = Power) as Brawl does no longer apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Using PFR Attributes doesn't mean you treat your character sheet as if it belonged to an ephemeral being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His defense is only 3 (lower of Power/Finesse) </div> </div> </div>See above; you don't lose your Skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and he has health 5 (Resolve 3 + 2 Lair). </div> </div> </div>Extra no. Your Attribute maximum is the higher of 5 and Lair, not Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:51:50-07:00","id":923996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=923978#post923978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Using PFR Attributes doesn't mean you treat your character sheet as if it belonged to an ephemeral being.<br /> <br /> See above; you don't lose your Skills.<br /> <br /> Extra no. Your Attribute maximum is the higher of 5 and Lair, not Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To apply that to the example character:<br /> <br /> Attacking with Brawl stays at 7 dice.<br /> <br /> Defense <b>Increases</b> to 6 (Because Finesse is equal to the highest finesse attribute instead of Wits for a Beast)<br /> <br /> And Health stays the same at 8.<br /> <br /> That's assuming that no Social Attributes are higher than Physical or Mental and that none of the extra Horror points were spent on attributes and all on size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:09:22-07:00","id":924006,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks for pointing that out. Only now do I realise that indeed only attributes are mentioned in the Dream Form / The Horror Itself section, and skills are not mentioned at all. I somehow assumed it was the same system as for ephimeral beings, who do not possess skills. And health is indeed resolve + trait max instead of simply lair. So you if you spend the four points to increase your strength, you get better combat dice for the horror. Also, you have an increased defense as pointed out above. On the other hand, you still cannot use Looming Presence to increase your health and still cannot use Nightmares if merged with your horror. But it makes much more sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:15:26-07:00","id":924010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=924006#post924006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks for pointing that out. Only now do I realise that indeed only attributes are mentioned in the Dream Form / The Horror Itself section, and skills are not mentioned at all. I somehow assumed it was the same system as for ephimeral beings, who do not possess skills. And health is indeed resolve + trait max instead of simply lair. So you if you spend the four points to increase your strength, you get better combat dice for the horror. Also, you have an increased defense as pointed out above. On the other hand, you still cannot use Looming Presence to increase your health and still cannot use Nightmares if merged with your horror. But it makes much more sense now.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it could have been clearer, it says nothing about being unable to use Nightmares if <b>merged</b> with your Horror. In fact, the paragraph that talks about it implies the opposite:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Horror Itself</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Beast enters her own Lair (or a Lair connected to it as a Brood Lair) via a Primordial Pathway, she immediately merges with her Horror. She likewise instantly separates if she uses a Pathway to leave. The Horror itself only leaves the Lair (barring Inheritance; see p. 234) when Starving or Ravenous, and no power can force it to do so in other circumstances. <b>When merged with the Horror, the Beast cannot choose to use the low Satiety version of her Atavisms unless her Satiety rating is actually low.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>While they should have been more clear, this tells me that a merged Beast is capable of using all of the tools at its disposal, including Nightmares, as if it weren't merged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:44:00-07:00","id":924107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests#post848254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, folks. I'm working on the outline for the <b>Beast Player's Guide</b> right now (it keeps getting pushed to the back burner because of <b>Changeling 20th</b>, but it's still...cooking, I guess). Obviously I'm looking at including the things you'll expect to find; new powers, approaches to play, expanded discussions on Families and Hungers and so forth. I'm interested in what <i>you</i> folks want to see in a Player's Guide. What would be useful for playing <b>Beast</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some more ativisms and nightmares would be cool. Maybe a base ability beasts can obtain by having kinship with other templates (like seeing ghosts in twilight with a sin-eater, spirits in twilight with a werewolf, able to benefit from goblin fruit from changelings )<br /> <br /> Most importantly I think the primordial dream can be elaborated on, maybe uses beasts can have for it outside of their own lair, being able to navigate it. Talk more about chambers that aren't connected to lair maybe and possible things beasts can do with them. Maybe have it populated by goeta which beasts can see and interact with. <br /> <br /> Lots of potential","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:20:50-07:00","id":924518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=924107#post924107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some more ativisms and nightmares would be cool. Maybe a base ability beasts can obtain by having kinship with other templates (like seeing ghosts in twilight with a sin-eater, spirits in twilight with a werewolf, able to benefit from goblin fruit from changelings )<br /> <br /> Most importantly I think the primordial dream can be elaborated on, maybe uses beasts can have for it outside of their own lair, being able to navigate it. Talk more about chambers that aren't connected to lair maybe and possible things beasts can do with them. Maybe have it populated by goeta which beasts can see and interact with.<br /> <br /> Lots of potential</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Though it would probably fit a Storytellers Guide more, it might be interesting to see what play <i>in</i> the Primordial Dream would be like. As in, the PD as a setting in itself, with a Brood investigating disused Chambers and other weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:43:43-07:00","id":924649,"title":"","content":"some Roleplaying advise at various points of Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:00:35-07:00","id":929076,"title":"","content":"How about nightmare ripples? When a beast traumatizes someone so much through a lesson that echos of the nightmare affect the whole area and make people heed the lesson?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T06:08:48-07:00","id":932481,"title":"","content":"Matt, is the outline done yet? Of so any chance of a preview? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:59:40-07:00","id":972269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=864047#post864047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, so, I have/had no intention of offending you, and I have no intention of pursuing this debate since I have little to no technical knowledge as to the intricacies of how sociopathic tendencies and psychopathy actually relate. However, I would posit that the traits you point out that you <i>don't </i>possess <i>are </i>those possessed by the True Fae. In fact, they're the traits that more or less <i>define </i>the True Fae. Also, the narrative constraints are being a little undersold here, I think. An Actor is stuck as that single story, and no matter how it is reshaped, it remains a single story. Self-direction, rationality, and efficiency go out the window when you need to abide by Frailties and are incapable of changing anything but the presentation of your core identity.<br /> <br /> That being said, from an objective stance, I can see how being a Changeling is desirable, and how it can be seen as a superior state to baseline humanity. The idea of a non-malicious Durance was discussed in the Changeling forums a while back, along with the social implications being one such lucky member of the Lost would have amongst others with a totally non-consensual stay in Faerie. That being said, I disagree that the True Fae are superior simply for raw power and immortality- barring things like Titles, I think it would be better to be a Wyrd 10 Changeling than a True Fae- at least you'd still have your free will. That being said, I'll leave the Changeling talk to the more well-informed, like Arc and Satchel.</div> </div> </div> </div> This assumes one believes in free will.<br /> <br /> I can see certain personalities finding becoming True Fae attractive, but most of those are not going to be pleasant people.<br /> <br /> I see far more people wanting the power of True Fae titles, but without having to give up their soul to become True Fae.<br /> <br /> I could see a Wyrd 10 Changeling putting themselves into an eternal dreaming state achiving something simular, basically treating their Dream Bastion like an Arcadian Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:04:25-07:00","id":972270,"title":"","content":"While this is more of a Storyteller's Guide thing, I'd love to see advice for a Beast chronicle that spends a lot of time in the Astral/Dream as an alternate structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:14:01-07:00","id":972278,"title":"","content":"Since we know we're getting Dark Mother cultists, what do you think we'll get on that front? Matt mentioned that he likes &quot;playable examples&quot;, so we're probably getting some sample groups and mechanical tips. Hopefully a sidebar or a note about how Beasts and mortal DM cultists interact with the Circle of the Crone, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:47:24-07:00","id":972488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests?p=924006#post924006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks for pointing that out. Only now do I realise that indeed only attributes are mentioned in the Dream Form / The Horror Itself section, and skills are not mentioned at all. I somehow assumed it was the same system as for ephimeral beings, who do not possess skills. And health is indeed resolve + trait max instead of simply lair. So you if you spend the four points to increase your strength, you get better combat dice for the horror. Also, you have an increased defense as pointed out above. On the other hand, you still cannot use Looming Presence to increase your health and still cannot use Nightmares if merged with your horror. But it makes much more sense now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd try to work in Looming Presence into granting those extra health levels for the Horror somehow. Just stack on the extra Size and health levels onto the track. It makes no sense for a supernatural power to just cease working when others of the same type still function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/